{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c623","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":364,"recorded_at":1780531400000723,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"c2010bc3-1267-4c2e-ba75-38fdaaeb742d"},"task_id":"c2010bc3-1267-4c2e-ba75-38fdaaeb742d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"c2010bc3-1267-4c2e-ba75-38fdaaeb742d","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2619 line(s) above)\n2620|## 7. Provider plugin protocol\n2621|\n2622|### 7.1 Discovery and trust\n2623|\n2624|Built-in support covers <code>codex</code>, <code>claude</code>,\n2625|<code>gemini</code>, <code>muse</code>, <code>antigravity</code>, and\n2626|<code>pi</code>. External provider executables are named\n2627|<code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code>, where <code>id</code> matches\n2628|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>.\n2629|\n2630|Candidate discovery order is:\n2631|\n2632|1. configured <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> in listed order;\n2633|2. built-in adapters; then\n2634|3. <code>PATH</code>, only when <code>allow_path_plugins</code> is true.\n2635|\n2636|M0 establishes the versioned plugin wire contracts, internal implementation\n2637|interfaces, and a conformance harness. M0 MUST NOT advertise a public stable\n2638|plugin SDK. A stable public SDK remains deferred until both Codex and Claude\n2639|implementations validate that the boundary is sufficient without provider-\n2640|specific authority leakage or compatibility shims.\n2641|\n2642|The order does not establish precedence. If two candidates—including a built-in\n2643|and an executable—declare the same provider ID, discovery MUST fail with\n2644|<code>invalid_config</code> before either candidate is probed or executed.\n2645|Configuration schema 1.0.0 has no duplicate-selection override; the operator\n2646|must remove or rename one candidate. For each accepted external candidate, the\n2647|canonical absolute executable path and SHA-256 digest MUST be recorded at trust\n2648|time. Symlinks MUST be resolved before comparison, the target MUST be a regular\n2649|file owned by the operator or an administrator-approved identity, and a changed\n2650|path target or digest MUST require renewed trust. Plugins execute with the\n2651|operator's privileges and are inside the trusted-host boundary, but they MUST\n2652|receive only the minimum operation-specific inputs.\n2653|\n2654|### 7.2 Framing and lifecycle\n2655|\n2656|The provider protocol is line-delimited JSON over stdin/stdout with\n2657|<code>protocol = \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\"</code> and\n2658|<code>protocol_version = \"2.0.0\"</code>. Each line MUST be one complete UTF-8\n2659|JSON object no larger than 8 MiB. Stdout MUST contain protocol frames only;\n2660|human diagnostics go to stderr.\n2661|\n2662|<code>ax</code> starts one plugin process per operation. Requests are\n2663|single-flight in v2. After one response, <code>ax</code> closes stdin and the\n2664|plugin MUST exit. Exit 0 requires a successful response. A structured error\n2665|response SHOULD exit 0 because the protocol succeeded; a crash, invalid frame,\n2666|or missing response is a provider-host failure.\n2667|\n2668|Request envelope:\n2669|\n2670|~~~json\n2671|{\n2672|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2673|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2674|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2675|  \"operation\": \"doctor\",\n2676|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:05:00.000Z\",\n2677|  \"body\": {\n2678|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2679|    \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2680|    \"provider_executable\": \"/opt/local/bin/pi\",\n2681|    \"identity\": null\n2682|  }\n2683|}\n2684|~~~\n2685|\n2686|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2687|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n2688|<code>operation</code> from the Section 7.5 operation registry,\n2689|<code>deadline</code> timestamp, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>.\n2690|The deadline MUST be in the future when the host writes the frame.\n2691|\n2692|Success envelope:\n2693|\n2694|~~~json\n2695|{\n2696|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2697|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2698|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2699|  \"ok\": true,\n2700|  \"body\": {\n2701|    \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2702|    \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2703|    \"findings\": []\n2704|  }\n2705|}\n2706|~~~\n2707|\n2708|A success envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2709|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>ok = true</code>,\n2710|and the operation-specific <code>body</code>. A failure envelope contains\n2711|exactly the first four members with <code>ok = false</code> plus\n2712|<code>error</code>, and MUST NOT contain <code>body</code>. Envelope and body\n2713|unknown members are protocol errors under major version 2.\n2714|\n2715|Failure envelope:\n2716|\n2717|~~~json\n2718|{\n2719|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2720|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2721|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2722|  \"ok\": false,\n2723|  \"error\": {\n2724|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n2725|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2726|    \"code\": \"capability_unavailable\",\n2727|    \"message\": \"portable store is not available for this provider build\",\n2728|    \"exit_code\": 6,\n2729|    \"retryable\": false,\n2730|    \"details\": {}\n2731|  }\n2732|}\n2733|~~~\n2734|\n2735|Provider protocol <code>2.x</code> statically binds every failure envelope to\n2736|Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>. The error schema is not independently\n2737|negotiated on a provider invocation; a provider-protocol minor that needs a\n2738|different error schema must explicitly revise that binding. Section 15.1\n2739|defines supported-major, unsupported-major, and invalid-first-frame behavior.\n2740|\n2741|The host MUST terminate a plugin that exceeds its deadline and report\n2742|<code>provider_timeout</code>. It MUST redact environment and stderr before\n2743|logging.\n2744|\n2745|### 7.3 Provider Manifest\n2746|\n2747|The <code>manifest</code> operation requires an empty body and returns\n2748|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2749|\n2750|~~~json\n2751|{\n2752|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest\",\n2753|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2754|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2755|  \"display_name\": \"Pi\",\n2756|  \"plugin_version\": \"0.1.0\",\n2757|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.73.1 <0.74.0\",\n2758|  \"platforms\": [\"linux\", \"macos\", \"windows\", \"wsl2\"],\n2759|  \"operations\": [\n2760|    \"manifest\",\n2761|    \"probe\",\n2762|    \"launch\",\n2763|    \"identify-session\",\n2764|    \"quiesce\",\n2765|    \"native-store-plan\",\n2766|    \"capture\",\n2767|    \"materialize\",\n2768|    \"materialize-status\",\n2769|    \"materialize-commit\",\n2770|    \"materialize-rollback\",\n2771|    \"resume\",\n2772|    \"fork\",\n2773|    \"stop\",\n2774|    \"doctor\"\n2775|  ],\n2776|  \"capability_names\": [\n2777|    \"native_resume\",\n2778|    \"portable_store\",\n2779|    \"managed_pty\",\n2780|    \"appserver\",\n2781|    \"task_board_primary\",\n2782|    \"prompt_spawn\",\n2783|    \"native_goal_binding\"\n2784|  ]\n2785|}\n2786|~~~\n2787|\n2788|The manifest is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2789|<code>display_name</code> is 1–128 UTF-8 characters;\n2790|<code>plugin_version</code> is SemVer; <code>provider_version_range</code> is a\n2791|1–256 character provider-adapter constraint; <code>platforms</code> is a sorted,\n2792|unique non-empty subset of the four platform enums; <code>operations</code> is\n2793|the ordered registry shown in Section 7.5 with no duplicates; and\n2794|<code>capability_names</code> is the exact seven-name ordered registry shown.\n2795|The manifest declares possible surfaces, not runtime availability.\n2796|\n2797|### 7.4 Capability result\n2798|\n2799|The <code>probe</code> operation body contains platform, architecture,\n2800|provider executable path, and requested capability names. Its response MUST\n2801|identify the exact provider version and emit every known capability using\n2802|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-probe</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2803|\n2804|~~~json\n2805|{\n2806|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-probe\",\n2807|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2808|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2809|  \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2810|  \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2811|  \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2812|  \"capabilities\": {\n2813|    \"native_resume\": {\n2814|      \"status\": \"available\",\n2815|      \"enabled\": true,\n2816|      \"evidence\": \"probed\",\n2817|      \"detail\": \"--session, --continue, and --resume are present\"\n2818|    },\n2819|    \"portable_store\": {\n2820|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2821|      \"enabled\": false,\n2822|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2823|      \"detail\": \"closed-store cross-host fixture has not passed\"\n2824|    },\n2825|    \"managed_pty\": {\n2826|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2827|      \"enabled\": false,\n2828|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2829|      \"detail\": \"platform PTY interruption and flush gate has not passed\"\n2830|    },\n2831|    \"appserver\": {\n2832|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2833|      \"enabled\": false,\n2834|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2835|      \"detail\": \"Pi RPC is not claimed as the ax appserver capability\"\n2836|    },\n2837|    \"task_board_primary\": {\n2838|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2839|      \"enabled\": false,\n2840|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2841|      \"detail\": \"no reliable primary adapter is accepted\"\n2842|    },\n2843|    \"prompt_spawn\": {\n2844|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2845|      \"enabled\": false,\n2846|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2847|      \"detail\": \"not claimed for v0.3.0\"\n2848|    },\n2849|    \"native_goal_binding\": {\n2850|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2851|      \"enabled\": false,\n2852|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2853|      \"detail\": \"no native task-board goal binding\"\n2854|    }\n2855|  },\n2856|  \"warnings\": []\n2857|}\n2858|~~~\n2859|\n2860|The probe object is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2861|<code>provider_version</code> is a 1–128 character exact version string,\n2862|architecture is <code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>, and\n2863|<code>capabilities</code> contains exactly the seven requested registry keys.\n2864|Each capability value contains exactly <code>status</code>,\n2865|<code>enabled</code>, <code>evidence</code>, and a 0–2,048 character\n2866|<code>detail</code>. <code>warnings</code> is a sorted, unique array of at most\n2867|1,024 strings of at most 2,048 characters each.\n2868|\n2869|Status is one of <code>available</code>, <code>conditional</code>,\n2870|<code>unsupported</code>, or <code>unknown</code>. Only\n2871|<code>available</code> MAY set <code>enabled</code> true. Evidence is one of\n2872|<code>documented</code>, <code>probed</code>, <code>accepted_test</code>,\n2873|<code>provider_contract</code>, <code>inferred</code>,\n2874|<code>acceptance_required</code>, or <code>none</code>.\n2875|\n2876|### 7.5 Required operations\n2877|\n2878|All plugins MUST implement every operation and return\n2879|<code>capability_unavailable</code> when the provider lacks the surface.\n2880|\n2881|Every request and success <code>body</code> is a closed object. The following\n2882|embedded types are part of provider protocol 2.0.0:\n2883|\n2884|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n2885|| --- | --- |\n2886|| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n2887|| <code>WorkspacePaths</code> | <code>map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]</code>; paths are destination-native, canonical, and contain no NUL |\n2888|| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\n2889|| <code>ProcessObservation</code> | <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>executable_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>candidate_store_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..256]</code>, <code>candidate_native_ids:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>; no PID is carried |\n2890|| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\n2891|| <code>SafeBoundaryProof</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean&#124;null</code>, <code>open_child_count:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handle_count:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique enum[0..5]</code> |\n2892|| <code>ValidationEvidence</code> | <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>status:passed&#124;skipped</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\n2893|| <code>NativeDiscoveryProof</code> | <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>discovered:boolean</code>, <code>discovery_root:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>backend_resolved:boolean</code> |\n2894|| <code>ProcessClosure</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n2895|| <code>DoctorFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>evidence:documented&#124;probed&#124;accepted_test&#124;provider_contract&#124;inferred&#124;acceptance_required&#124;none</code> |\n2896|| <code>ProviderStoreAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>access:capture_source&#124;materialize_destination</code> |\n2897|| <code>AuthorityTarget</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>relative_path:.&#124;path</code> |\n2898|| <code>ProviderCaptureItem</code> | <code>source_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>source_relative_path:path</code>, <code>manifest_path:path</code>, <code>kind:file&#124;directory</code>, <code>state_class:durable_payload&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>required:boolean</code> |\n2899|| <code>ProviderCapturePlan</code> | <code>capture_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_authorities:ProviderStoreAuthority[1..32]</code>, <code>items:ProviderCaptureItem[1..32768]</code>, <code>excluded_targets:AuthorityTarget[0..4096]</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, <code>snapshot_requires_closed_store:boolean</code> |\n2900|| <code>ObjectSink</code> | <code>root:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>create_mode:exclusive</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2901|| <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_objects</code>, <code>kind:provider_object_source</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>access:read_only</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2902|| <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>kind:provider_transaction</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:provider_transaction_v1</code>, <code>access:read_write</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids:sorted unique root-id[1..32]</code> |\n2903|| <code>ProviderTransactionEntry</code> | <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>provider_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>target_relative_path:path</code>, <code>expected_prior_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>prior_kind:absent&#124;file&#124;directory&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>backup_relative_path:path&#124;null</code>, <code>applied:boolean</code>, <code>restored:boolean</code> |\n2904|| <code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code> | <code>protocol:urn:ax:protocol:provider</code>, <code>protocol_version:2.0.0</code>, <code>document_kind:materialization_transaction</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>state:preparing&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;committed&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>entries:ProviderTransactionEntry[1..65536]</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp</code>, <code>terminal_at:timestamp&#124;null</code> |\n2905|| <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>state:unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code> |\n2906|\n2907|The <code>SafeBoundaryProof.blockers</code> enum is\n2908|<code>background_unproven</code>, <code>child_process_open</code>,\n2909|<code>database_handle_open</code>, <code>provider_busy</code>, or\n2910|<code>store_unstable</code>. A safe proof requires empty blockers,\n2911|<code>input_blocked</code>, <code>foreground_idle</code>,\n2912|<code>background_idle = true</code>, both counts zero, and non-null boundary and\n2913|store generation. <code>ValidationEvidence</code> arrays MUST be sorted by\n2914|<code>code</code> with no duplicate code. Opaque process handles are valid only\n2915|for the operation lifetime and MUST NOT be persisted or replicated.\n2916|\n2917|The <code>root-id</code> grammar is\n2918|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code>. Capture authorities are sorted by\n2919|<code>authority_id</code>, have <code>access = capture_source</code>, and are\n2920|unique. Capture items are sorted by <code>manifest_path</code>; each authority\n2921|reference MUST resolve, and\n2922|<code>root_path/source_relative_path</code> MUST remain under that exact root\n2923|after symlink/reparse-point resolution. Items MUST neither overlap nor traverse\n2924|through a symlink. Excluded targets are sorted by authority ID then relative\n2925|path and MUST reference the same authority set. <code>derived_cache</code> is\n2926|included only when Section 8 identifies it as required discovery metadata;\n2927|otherwise it must be excluded. Provider roots that contain credentials,\n2928|machine authentication, runtime sockets, locks, or live ax state MUST be\n2929|rejected even when a plugin names them. <code>ObjectSink.root</code> is a fresh owner-only directory\n2930|created by <code>ax</code>. Under <code>sha256_loose_v1</code>, a plugin writes\n2931|each complete blob with create-new semantics at\n2932|the exact Section 3.2 <code>digest_path_v1</code> relative path\n2933|<code>sha256/HH/REST</code> (two-hex shard, 62-hex leaf).\n2934|It MUST NOT create symlinks, hardlinks, devices, sockets, or any file not named\n2935|by its returned descriptors. The host independently hashes every sink file,\n2936|checks size/limits/exclusions, and only then imports it into the ax object\n2937|store. A plugin never receives the live object-store root.\n2938|\n2939|The destination host, not the peer and not the plugin, constructs both\n2940|materialization authorities. A <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority.root_path</code>\n2941|MUST equal\n2942|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-object-sources/&lt;materialization-id&gt;/&lt;provider-id&gt;</code>;\n2943|it is a fresh owner-only directory containing exactly the verified manifest\n2944|closure at the same <code>digest_path_v1</code> paths. The host makes every file read-only\n2945|before invoking the plugin. The authority's manifest IDs, byte/blob limits,\n2946|materialization ID, and provider ID MUST equal the selected checkpoint and\n2947|plan. An extra file, writable file, symlink, digest mismatch, or path supplied\n2948|by a remote request is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n2949|\n2950|A <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path</code> MUST equal\n2951|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-transactions/&lt;provider-id&gt;/&lt;transaction-id&gt;</code>.\n2952|It is a fresh owner-only directory, is disjoint from the object source and all\n2953|plan roots, and names exactly the materialization/provider/transaction/plan in\n2954|the authority. Its\n2955|<code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids</code> MUST equal the sorted set of\n2956|all <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority IDs used by plan operations. The\n2957|host MUST prove that the transaction root and every named provider-store root\n2958|are on the same filesystem/volume before the first plugin mutation. If one is\n2959|not, provider protocol 2.0.0 fails with <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>; it MUST\n2960|NOT fall back to an in-place cross-filesystem copy.\n2961|\n2962|The <code>provider_transaction_v1</code> layout contains only these durable\n2963|paths, plus one same-directory temporary file while atomically replacing\n2964|<code>transaction.json</code>:\n2965|\n2966|~~~text\n2967|transaction.json\n2968|staged/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2969|backups/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2970|~~~\n2971|\n2972|<code>transaction.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the closed\n2973|<code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code>. Entries are sorted by sequence and\n2974|are exactly the provider-store operations in the plan. For a pre-existing\n2975|target, <code>backup_relative_path</code> is exactly\n2976|<code>backups/&lt;provider-authority-id&gt;/&lt;operation-sequence&gt;</code>; an absent\n2977|target requires <code>prior_kind = absent</code>, a null backup path, and a null\n2978|expected prior digest. Every other prior kind requires that exact non-null\n2979|backup path and a non-null expected prior digest. A prepared document has every\n2980|entry applied, no entry restored, a non-null rollback token, and non-null native\n2981|discovery. A committed document keeps the applied facts, sets the token to\n2982|null, removes every staged/backup payload from disk, and has non-null\n2983|discovery. A rolled-\n2984|back document has every pre-existing entry restored, every transaction-created\n2985|target removed, a null token, and discovery describing the restored\n2986|destination. The plugin MUST fsync a staged replacement and the\n2987|transaction document, atomically rename any predecessor into its backup, then\n2988|atomically rename the staged replacement into the exact target. Each document\n2989|transition is written to a fresh temporary regular file, fsynced, renamed over\n2990|<code>transaction.json</code>, and followed by a parent-directory fsync where\n2991|the platform supports it. Windows uses replace/write-through semantics with\n2992|equivalent user-only DACLs.\n2993|\n2994|<code>terminal_at</code> is null in <code>preparing</code>,\n2995|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n2996|<code>rolling_back</code> states and non-null in\n2997|<code>committed|rolled_back</code> states.\n2998|<code>updated_at</code> never precedes <code>created_at</code>, and terminal time\n2999|never precedes either. Timestamps are diagnostics; state, IDs, entry facts, and\n3000|filesystem verification decide recovery.\n3001|\n3002|Every transaction operation receives the same complete\n3003|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>. A fresh plugin process locates state\n3004|only through that authority, validates the path and\n3005|<code>transaction.json</code> IDs before acting, and MUST NOT use an ambient\n3006|transaction registry or search another root. A crash while\n3007|<code>preparing</code>, <code>committing</code>, or <code>rolling_back</code> is\n3008|reconciled from the entries to one exposed status before\n3009|<code>materialize-status</code> responds; an irreconcilable entry is\n3010|<code>integrity_failure</code> and retains the root for diagnosis. Prepared\n3011|documents store the rollback token under owner-only permissions so a later\n3012|process can reconstruct the current durable status; terminal documents set it\n3013|to null.\n3014|Commit removes all backups only after durable committed state; rollback\n3015|restores all predecessors before durable rolled-back state. The terminal\n3016|<code>transaction.json</code> receipt remains until the corresponding\n3017|Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\n3018|<code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> afterward. Object-source bytes and\n3019|backup/staged subtrees MAY then be removed; live or ambiguous roots MUST NOT be\n3020|garbage-collected.\n3021|\n3022|In <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code>, <code>unknown</code> requires null\n3023|plan/token/discovery; <code>prepared</code> requires all three non-null;\n3024|<code>committed</code> and <code>rolled_back</code> require a non-null plan and\n3025|discovery proof and a null rollback token. The discovery proof in a rolled-back\n3026|status describes the destination after rollback. An operation failure does not\n3027|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n3028|status request reports the last durable state. An unreadable or\n3029|integrity-invalid transaction MUST fail with <code>integrity_failure</code> and\n3030|MUST be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status object.\n3031|Every provider mutation request that carries <code>operation_id</code> uses the\n3032|single Provider protocol 2.0.0 idempotency key\n3033|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>. An\n3034|identical canonical mutation request MUST return a byte-identical result across\n3035|a fresh plugin process; any changed member is\n3036|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and MUST cause no new mutation. Observational\n3037|operations, including <code>materialize-status</code>, are evolving reads. They\n3038|use the provider envelope's fresh <code>request_id</code> only for correlation,\n3039|MUST NOT be stored as mutation receipts, and MUST return the durable state at\n3040|the read's reconciliation point even when an earlier identical read returned a\n3041|different phase. For <code>capture</code>, replay verifies/reuses only exact\n3042|digest-named files already present in the same Object Sink and re-emits the\n3043|same manifest/descriptors; an extra or changed file fails integrity. Provider\n3044|<code>fork</code> is side-effect-free and recomputes the same plan. The\n3045|materialize mutations use their durable transaction document as the receipt.\n3046|No operation relies on a searched ambient registry. Transaction IDs and\n3047|mutation operation IDs are caller-supplied and stable across retries. For one\n3048|provider materialization transaction, the <code>operation_id</code> is\n3049|transaction-wide across <code>materialize</code> and exactly one terminal\n3050|<code>materialize-commit</code> or <code>materialize-rollback</code>; a\n3051|<code>materialize-status</code> request omits it and locates the transaction only\n3052|through the caller-supplied materialization/transaction IDs and exact authority.\n3053|Reusing the mutation value across distinct operation tags does not alias their\n3054|recorded results. Within one provider ID,\n3055|an operation ID used by the materialize family identifies exactly one materialization transaction:\n3056|its <code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, plan ID, object\n3057|source, transaction authority, provider-store authorities, lease, activation,\n3058|rollback reason, and all remaining body members are immutable retry input for\n3059|their operation tag. Reusing <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> with any\n3060|different canonical body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>; the plugin MUST\n3061|return the first recorded result or failure and MUST NOT allocate, search, or\n3062|mutate another transaction root. A transaction or materialization ID already\n3063|bound to another operation ID is also <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. There\n3064|is no second tuple- or path-based idempotency key in provider protocol 2.0.0.\n3065|\n3066|The operation body registry is exact. A named schema object means the complete\n3067|validated object, not only its digest. Arrays of schema objects are sorted by\n3068|their canonical identity field and contain no duplicate identity:\n3069|\n3070|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3071|| --- | --- | --- |\n3072|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Provider Manifest object (Section 7.3) |\n3073|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\n3074|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3075|| <code>identify-session</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7, provider_id:provider-id, observation:ProcessObservation}</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak, matched_evidence:sorted unique native_id&#124;store_path&#124;provider_event&#124;backend_lookup[1..4]}</code> |\n3076|| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\n3077|| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, materialization_plan:Materialization Plan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], path_key_rewrites:map(UUIDv7,string[1..1024])[0..256]}</code> |\n3078|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, proof:SafeBoundaryProof, object_sink:ObjectSink, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_id:UUIDv7, manifest:Transfer Manifest, blob_descriptors:sorted unique Blob Descriptor[0..32768], written_blob_ids:sorted unique digest[0..32768], captured_store_generation:string[1..512], exclusions_applied:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code> |\n3079|| <code>materialize</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan:Materialization Plan, object_source:ProviderObjectSourceAuthority, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:prepared, created_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], merged_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], validations:ValidationEvidence[1..256], rollback_token:base64url-256+, native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof}</code> |\n3080|| <code>materialize-status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority}</code> | <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> |\n3081|| <code>materialize-commit</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, activation:dormant_validated&#124;owner_resumed, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:committed, backup_removed:boolean, committed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n3082|| <code>materialize-rollback</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:rolled_back, restored_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], removed_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], native_discovery_absent:boolean}</code> |\n3083|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3084|| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\n3085|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, mode:graceful&#124;force, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{closure:ProcessClosure}</code> |\n3086|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, identity:Provider Identity Record&#124;null}</code> | <code>{provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128]&#124;null, findings:DoctorFinding[0..1024]}</code> |\n3087|\n3088|For <code>launch</code>, the profile and launch plan MUST exactly equal their\n3089|Session Record values. Provider <code>fork</code> is a planning call: it MUST\n3090|NOT write a provider store, allocate an active backend conversation, or start a\n3091|process. Its operation ID is the Session Record's\n3092|<code>fork_provenance.operation_id</code>; an identical retry returns the same\n3093|plan and any changed body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. The new record\n3094|MUST contain Fork Provenance matching the source/checkpoint and operation, and\n3095|a successful result requires <code>provenance_verified = true</code> and MUST\n3096|NOT describe a blank session. <code>native_fork</code> requires\n3097|<code>requires_provider_materialization = false</code> and MAY have a planned\n3098|native ID when the provider allocates it only at process start.\n3099|<code>supported_import</code> requires\n3100|<code>requires_provider_materialization = true</code>; the coordinator then\n3101|calls <code>native-store-plan phase=materialize</code> with\n3102|<code>mode=fork</code> and includes the validated provider plan in the\n3103|destination materialization transaction. In both variants, a new Provider\n3104|Identity Record is authoritative only after native discovery following the\n3105|prepared transaction; the planned ID is an expectation, not an identity\n3106|record.\n3107|\n3108|<code>launch</code>, <code>resume</code>, and <code>fork</code> return plans; the\n3109|trusted terminal backend performs process creation. Plugins MUST NOT return\n3110|secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\n3111|advertised portable-store tuple and MUST separate durable includes,\n3112|machine-local excludes, path-key rewrites, quiescence preconditions, and\n3113|validation steps. Its two request and result variants are closed and disjoint:\n3114|a capture request has no destination platform, destination host, destination\n3115|workspace map, or source manifest; a materialize request has no source\n3116|workspace map. Capture therefore works for the first local checkpoint without\n3117|inventing a destination peer or a source-as-destination sentinel.\n3118|\n3119|The capture result's authorities are the complete provider source-root\n3120|authority for that capture. A materialize plan MUST contain at least one\n3121|Section 10.5 <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority with\n3122|<code>prepared_for_host_id = destination_host_id</code>. Every such authority\n3123|MUST have the same provider/platform as the request, resolve to a\n3124|destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\n3125|disjoint from ax data/state/cache/runtime roots, task-board staging,\n3126|workspaces, and credential/authentication roots unless an exact child path is\n3127|the provider's documented durable store. A path-key rewrite is keyed by logical\n3128|workspace ID and contains destination-derived non-secret cache-key data, never\n3129|a source absolute path. An unavailable surface returns the common failure\n3130|envelope, not a success body with a null required plan.\n3131|\n3132|The following source-only first-checkpoint body and result are the normative\n3133|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-POS</code> fixture. Their absence of every\n3134|destination member is intentional:\n3135|\n3136|~~~json\n3137|{\n3138|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3139|  \"identity\": {\n3140|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3141|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3142|    \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3143|    \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3144|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3145|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3146|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3147|    \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3148|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3149|    \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3150|    \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3151|    \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3152|    \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3153|    \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3154|    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3155|    \"extensions\": {}\n3156|  },\n3157|  \"source_platform\": \"macos\",\n3158|  \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3159|  \"source_workspace_paths\": {\n3160|    \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/payments-api\"\n3161|  },\n3162|  \"lease\": {\n3163|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3164|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n3165|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3166|  }\n3167|}\n3168|~~~\n3169|\n3170|~~~json\n3171|{\n3172|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3173|  \"capture_plan\": {\n3174|    \"capture_id\": \"0198f4c8-0790-72aa-8374-3234567890ab\",\n3175|    \"source_authorities\": [\n3176|      {\n3177|        \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3178|        \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3179|        \"platform\": \"macos\",\n3180|        \"root_path\": \"/Users/iv/.codex/sessions\",\n3181|        \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n3182|        \"access\": \"capture_source\"\n3183|      }\n3184|    ],\n3185|    \"items\": [\n3186|      {\n3187|        \"source_authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3188|        \"source_relative_path\": \"2026/08/19/rollout-11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555.jsonl\",\n3189|        \"manifest_path\": \"session/rollout.jsonl\",\n3190|        \"kind\": \"file\",\n3191|        \"state_class\": \"durable_payload\",\n3192|        \"required\": true\n3193|      }\n3194|    ],\n3195|    \"excluded_targets\": [],\n3196|    \"store_generation\": \"closed:11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555:1\",\n3197|    \"snapshot_requires_closed_store\": true\n3198|  },\n3199|  \"include_classes\": [\"durable_payload\"],\n3200|  \"exclude_classes\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"]\n3201|}\n3202|~~~\n3203|\n3204|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N1</code> adds\n3205|<code>destination_platform</code> to the capture body and MUST fail with\n3206|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\n3207|the item authority to an undeclared ID and MUST fail before any provider byte\n3208|is read. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N3</code> makes the source authority equal\n3209|the credential root and MUST fail with <code>secret_policy_violation</code>.\n3210|\n3211|<code>capture</code> is the only provider operation that may emit provider\n3212|payload bytes. It requires <code>proof.safe = true</code>, equal proof/plan store\n3213|generation, and the current lease. Its manifest MUST have\n3214|<code>kind = provider</code>, the session as subject, and exactly the returned\n3215|descriptor/blob closure. The host MUST reject an extra sink file, missing\n3216|required item, descriptor mismatch, excluded class/path, generation change, or\n3217|secret-policy violation and MUST discard the isolated sink without importing\n3218|it. The plugin MUST NOT write a live ax store, live SQLite index, credential\n3219|root, or destination native store during capture.\n3220|\n3221|Provider materialization is a recoverable two-decision transaction.\n3222|<code>materialize</code> applies the exact plan while retaining every replaced\n3223|destination byte under the authorized transaction layout and returns\n3224|<code>state = prepared</code>; it MUST NOT delete its backup. While prepared,\n3225|the host validates exact native discovery and either keeps the replica dormant\n3226|or starts the winning owner. It then calls <code>materialize-commit</code> to\n3227|discard the backup, or <code>materialize-rollback</code> to restore it. Commit\n3228|requires <code>backup_removed = true</code>; rollback requires the native\n3229|identity introduced by the transaction to be absent afterward unless it was a\n3230|pre-existing backend identity. A rollback token is machine-local recovery\n3231|authority, MUST be at least 256 random bits, MUST be stored only in the\n3232|owner-only Materialization Journal and prepared Provider Transaction Document,\n3233|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n3234|\n3235|The provider plugin MUST execute only plan operations whose authority has\n3236|<code>kind = provider_store</code> and whose <code>provider_id</code> equals the\n3237|plugin manifest ID. The ax host executes workspace and task-board operations;\n3238|it MUST reject a plugin response that reports any created or merged path\n3239|outside the selected provider-store authorities. The plugin resolves each\n3240|reported absolute path from that authority's root plus the operation's\n3241|relative target, rechecks the predecessor immediately before mutation, and\n3242|uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\n3243|transaction containing disjoint authority-specific executors, not a grant for\n3244|the provider plugin to mutate the workspace.\n3245|\n3246|The three mutation operations use the same parent <code>operation_id</code>,\n3247|<code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, and byte-identical\n3248|transaction authority. The sole mutation idempotency key remains\n3249|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>; the materialization and transaction IDs\n3250|are immutable non-key inputs. Each mutation tag therefore has a distinct key\n3251|while all phases locate the same authority. A retry of one mutation name MUST\n3252|use byte-identical canonical arguments. <code>materialize-status</code> omits\n3253|<code>operation_id</code>; it is the required evolving lost-response recovery\n3254|read and uses the envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation. A status\n3255|read MUST reconcile and return the current durable state, so a read that once\n3256|returned <code>prepared</code> may later return <code>committed</code> or\n3257|<code>rolled_back</code>. An unknown transaction MUST return state\n3258|<code>unknown</code>; the host MUST NOT infer success. A prepared transaction\n3259|survives plugin/host restart until explicit commit or rollback. A plugin that\n3260|cannot provide this prepare/status/commit/rollback behavior MUST advertise\n3261|<code>portable_store</code> disabled.\n3262|\n3263|Normative prepared result body:\n3264|\n3265|~~~json\n3266|{\n3267|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3268|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n3269|  \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n3270|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n3271|  \"state\": \"prepared\",\n3272|  \"created_paths\": [\"/srv/provider/sessions/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"],\n3273|  \"merged_paths\": [],\n3274|  \"validations\": [\n3275|    {\"code\":\"native_discovery\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"detail\":\"exact session identity resolved\"}\n3276|  ],\n3277|  \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n3278|  \"native_discovery\": {\n3279|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3280|    \"discovered\": true,\n3281|    \"discovery_root\": \"/srv/provider/sessions\",\n3282|    \"backend_resolved\": false\n3283|  }\n3284|}\n3285|~~~\n3286|\n3287|The normative transaction cases are:\n3288|\n3289|| Fixture | Calls | Required terminal state |\n3290|| --- | --- | --- |\n3291|| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\n3292|| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\n3293|| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\n3294|| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\n3295|| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\n3296|| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\n3297|| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\n3298|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\n3299|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\n3300|\n3301|Changing a plan, object-source authority, or transaction authority on a repeated\n3302|<code>materialize</code>, changing activation/lease on a repeated commit, or\n3303|changing rollback reason/token on a repeated rollback while reusing the same\n3304|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code> key is the normative negative\n3305|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\n3306|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3307|\n3308|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\n3309|same <code>(materialize, operation_id)</code> while changing only\n3310|<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\n3311|<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\n3312|one authority root. Each MUST return <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, leave the\n3313|original transaction document/root byte-identical, and create no second root.\n3314|\n3315|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3316|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3317|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3318|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3319|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3320|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3321|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3322|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3323|\n3324|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3325|\n3326|~~~json\n3327|{\n3328|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3329|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3330|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3331|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3332|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3333|  \"body\": {\n3334|    \"identity\": {\n3335|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3336|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3337|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3338|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3339|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3340|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3341|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3342|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3343|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3344|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3345|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3346|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3347|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3348|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3349|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3350|      \"extensions\": {}\n3351|    },\n3352|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3353|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3354|    },\n3355|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3356|    \"terminal\": {\n3357|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3358|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3359|      \"interactive\": true,\n3360|      \"columns\": 120,\n3361|      \"rows\": 40\n3362|    },\n3363|    \"lease\": {\n3364|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3365|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3366|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3367|    }\n3368|  }\n3369|}\n3370|~~~\n3371|\n3372|~~~json\n3373|{\n3374|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3375|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3376|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3377|  \"ok\": true,\n3378|  \"body\": {\n3379|    \"argv\": [\n3380|      \"codex\",\n3381|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3382|      \"resume\",\n3383|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3384|    ],\n3385|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3386|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3387|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3388|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3389|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3390|    \"extensions\": {}\n3391|  }\n3392|}\n3393|~~~\n3394|\n3395|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3396|\n3397|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3398|\n3399|- provider ID and exact version;\n3400|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3401|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3402|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3403|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3404|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3405|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3406|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3407|\n3408|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3409|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3410|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3411|request.\n3412|\n3413|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3414|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3415|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3416|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3417|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3418|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3419|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3420|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3421|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3422|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3423|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3424|\n3425|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3426|\n3427|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3428|\n3429|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3430|| --- | --- |\n3431|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3432|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3433|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3434|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3435|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3436|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3437|\n3438|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3439|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3440|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3441|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3442|probe accepts them.\n3443|\n3444|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3445|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3446|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3447|confirmation controls still apply.\n3448|\n3449|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3450|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3451|\n3452|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3453|\n3454|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3455|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3456|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3457|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3458|\n3459|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3460|| --- | --- |\n3461|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3462|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3463|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3464|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3465|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3466|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3467|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3468|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3469|\n3470|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3471|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3472|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3473|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3474|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3475|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3476|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3477|\n3478|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3479|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3480|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3481|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3482|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3483|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3484|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3485|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3486|\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3522|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3523|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3524|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3525|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3526|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3527|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3528|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3529|every candidate object.\n3530|\n3531|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3532|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3533|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3534|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3535|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3536|\n3537|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3538|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3539|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3540|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3541|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3542|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3543|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3544|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3545|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3546|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3547|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3548|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3549|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3550|  never paths.\n3551|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3552|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3553|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3554|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3555|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3556|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3557|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3558|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3559|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3560|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3561|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3562|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3563|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3564|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3565|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3566|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3567|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3568|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3569|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3570|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3571|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3572|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3573|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3574|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3575|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3576|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3577|\n3578|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3579|\n3580|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3581|| --- | --- | --- |\n3582|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3583|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3584|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3585|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3586|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3587|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3588|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3589|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3590|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3591|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3592|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3593|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3594|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3595|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3596|\n3597|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3598|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3599|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3600|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3601|and never fallback permission.\n3602|\n3603|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3604|\n3605|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3606|| --- | --- |\n3607|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3608|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3609|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3610|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3611|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3612|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3613|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3614|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3615|\n3616|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3617|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3618|\n3619|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3620|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3621|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3622|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3623|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3624|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3625|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3626|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3627|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3628|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3629|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3630|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3631|never contains executable provenance.\n3632|\n3633|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3634|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3635|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3636|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3637|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3638|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3639|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3640|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3641|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3642|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3643|\n3644|Each capability value contains exactly\n3645|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3646|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3647|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3648|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3649|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3650|\n3651|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3652|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3653|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3654|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3655|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3656|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3657|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3658|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3659|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3660|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3661|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3662|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3663|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3664|\n3665|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3666|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3667|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3668|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3669|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3670|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3671|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3672|write.\n3673|\n3674|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3675|\n3676|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3677|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3678|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3679|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3680|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3681|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3682|\n3683|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3684|\n3685|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3686|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3687|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3688|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3689|\n3690|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3691|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3692|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3693|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3694|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3695|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3696|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3697|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3698|shared.\n3699|\n3700|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3701|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3702|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3703|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3704|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3705|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3706|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3707|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3708|uses an empty body.\n3709|\n3710|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3711|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3712|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3713|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3714|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3715|Error 1.2 has\n3716|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n3717|<code>retryable=false</code>, and then exit with status 6. Only that complete\n3718|response-plus-exit tuple authorizes the caller to launch a fresh process for\n3719|the next lower locally supported major. The response is negotiation evidence,\n3720|not trusted manifest data and not an ordinary retryable operation failure.\n3721|\n3722|Success requires one well-framed success response with every echo exact, a\n3723|complete schema-valid manifest whose <code>supported_protocol_versions</code>\n3724|contains the exact selected version, and process exit 0. A wrong or missing\n3725|echo, malformed/partial/extra frame, invalid UTF-8/JSON/schema, timeout,\n3726|signal, nonmatching exit status, authentication/allowlist failure, integrity\n3727|failure, or any error other than the exact downgrade tuple is terminal and\n3728|MUST NOT cause a lower-major attempt. The caller MUST NOT reinterpret a frame,\n3729|manifest, platform token, request body, or error from one major as another.\n3730|If every locally supported major returns the exact downgrade tuple, the caller\n3731|terminates with its own Structured Error 1.2\n3732|<code>incompatible_protocol</code>, exit 6, and no trusted manifest or partial\n3733|result. These rules select v2 directly, permit v2-to-v1 fallback, support a\n3734|v1-only caller/peer, and terminate deterministically when no major is common.\n3735|\n3736|Transport is one request and one response as line-delimited JSON over\n3737|authenticated local stdio or allowlisted AX SSH. One line is at most 8 MiB.\n3738|The request envelope contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n3739|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>protocol</code>,\n3740|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3741|<code>operation</code>, <code>deadline_ms:uint53[1..3600000]</code>, and the\n3742|closed operation <code>body</code>. The response echoes protocol/version,\n3743|request/operation. A success response contains exactly the common envelope\n3744|members, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>, with no <code>error</code>\n3745|member. A failure response contains exactly the common envelope members,\n3746|<code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.2.0 in <code>error</code>, with no\n3747|<code>body</code> member. Unknown fields, both or neither branch members, invalid\n3748|UTF-8/JSON, multiple frames, wrong echo, oversize, timeout, or exit without one\n3749|valid response fail with no partial trusted data. Stdout is protocol-only;\n3750|redacted diagnostics use stderr.\n3751|\n3752|The Directory Node Manifest contains exactly schema/version,\n3753|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3754|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3755|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3756|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3757|<code>supported_protocol_versions:sorted unique SemVer[1..16]</code>,\n3758|<code>operations:sorted unique DirectoryNodeOperation[11]</code>,\n3759|<code>schemas:sorted unique ContractAssertion[15..64]</code>,\n3760|<code>environment_tuple_registry_id:digest</code>,\n3761|<code>capabilities:map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult)[8]</code>,\n3762|<code>redaction_policy_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n3763|<code>enrichment_profile_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>,\n3764|<code>limits:DirectoryNodeLimits</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. The three\n3765|façade executable/module bindings and tuple declarations MUST agree; a\n3766|contradiction is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3767|\n3768|<code>CapabilityResult</code> contains exactly\n3769|<code>status:available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code>,\n3770|<code>reason_code:string[1..128]|null</code>,\n3771|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>,\n3772|<code>observed_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Available has a\n3773|null reason; every other status requires one. <code>DirectoryNodeLimits</code>\n3774|contains exactly <code>max_frame_bytes:uint53[1..8388608]</code>,\n3775|<code>max_scan_instances:uint53[1..65536]</code>,\n3776|<code>max_inventory_take:uint53[1..1000]</code>,\n3777|<code>max_excerpt_count:uint53[0..20]</code>,\n3778|<code>max_excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096]</code>,\n3779|<code>max_enrichment_events:uint53[1..5000]</code>,\n3780|<code>max_enrichment_bytes:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n3781|<code>extensions</code>. Both nested objects are closed except for their listed\n3782|reverse-DNS extension maps.\n3783|\n3784|The exact operation registry and bodies are:\n3785|\n3786|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body | Mutation |\n3787|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3788|| <code>manifest</code> | empty object | complete Directory Node Manifest | none |\n3789|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,architecture:amd64\\|arm64,requested_environment_ids:sorted unique environment-id[0..64],requested_capabilities:sorted unique directory-capability[0..8],extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,node_build:DirectoryNodeBuild,policy_digest:digest,environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..256],findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code> | none |\n3790|| <code>scan</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],prior_batch_id:digest|null,cursor:string[1..4096]|null,max_instances:uint53[1..65536],extensions}</code> | <code>{batch:InventoryBatch,environment_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],native_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,extensions}</code> | directory records only |\n3791|| <code>inventory</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],fields:sorted unique observation-field[1..32],after:string[1..4096]|null,take:uint53[1..1000],extensions}</code> | <code>{observations:NativeSessionObservation[0..1000],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code> | none |\n3792|| <code>preview</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,roles:sorted unique user\\|assistant[1..2],excerpt_count:uint53[0..20],excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096],redaction_policy_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,instance_id:digest,observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,excerpts:PreviewExcerpt[0..20],truncated:boolean,redaction_summary:RedactionSummary,freshness:DirectoryFreshness,extensions}</code> | none |\n3793|| <code>enrichment-plan</code> | <code>{request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{accepted:boolean,expected_input_events:uint53,expected_input_bytes:uint53,expected_model_calls:uint53,disclosure_classes:sorted unique string[0..64],blockers:sorted unique string[0..128],extensions}</code> | none |\n3794|| <code>enrichment-run</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | annotation/job records only |\n3795|| <code>enrichment-status</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,receipt_chain_ids:digest[1..4096],produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | none |\n3796|| <code>continuation-inspect</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,management_binding:ManagementBinding,safe_boundary_status:proven\\|unproven\\|not_required,runtime_status:RuntimeExpectation,warnings:sorted unique string[0..256],extensions}</code> | none |\n3797|| <code>runtime-observe</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{runtime:RuntimeExpectation,extensions}</code> | none |\n3798|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256],include_conformance_age:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{healthy:boolean,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],environment_capabilities:map(digest,map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult))[0..256],cloning_contracts:sorted unique ContractAssertion[0..64],extensions}</code> | none |\n3799|\n3800|Each displayed body is closed; its member types, ordering, and limits are the\n3801|registered Section 10.8 schemas and manifest bounds. The <code>probe</code> row\n3802|shown above is the Request 2.0.0 form; Request 1.0.0 differs only in its closed\n3803|legacy platform vocabulary recorded in the major-binding table. The capability\n3804|registry is exactly <code>directory_discovery</code>,\n3805|<code>directory_incremental_scan</code>, <code>directory_head_digest</code>,\n3806|<code>directory_tail_preview</code>, <code>native_title_read</code>,\n3807|<code>native_runtime_observation</code>,\n3808|<code>existing_session_adoption</code>, and <code>native_resume</code>.\n3809|The closed <code>observation-field</code> registry is exactly\n3810|<code>identity</code>, <code>management</code>, <code>head</code>,\n3811|<code>state</code>, <code>workspace</code>, <code>title</code>,\n3812|<code>counts</code>, <code>preview_status</code>, <code>warnings</code>, and\n3813|<code>timestamps</code>. <code>PreviewExcerpt</code> contains exactly\n3814|<code>role:user|assistant</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n3815|<code>text:string[0..4096]</code>, <code>source_event_id:digest</code>,\n3816|<code>truncated:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3817|<code>ManagementBinding</code> contains exactly\n3818|<code>state:managed|unmanaged|conflicted</code>,\n3819|<code>session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n3820|<code>provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n3821|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n3822|<code>extensions</code>; both IDs and non-empty evidence are required exactly\n3823|for managed, both IDs are null for unmanaged, and conflicted retains all\n3824|evidence without choosing a winner. These nested objects are closed except for\n3825|their listed extension maps. <code>DirectoryNodeBuild</code> contains exactly\n3826|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3827|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3828|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3829|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3830|<code>extensions</code>; every value equals the current manifest.\n3831|Discovery may degrade for an unknown source tuple only when stable identity and\n3832|bounds remain safe; head/preview/resume/adoption/write/launch fail closed.\n3833|\n3834|<code>scan</code> and <code>enrichment-run</code> use\n3835|<code>(operation,operation_id)</code> idempotency. Repeating the same canonical\n3836|body returns the prior durable result; a changed body is\n3837|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> without new records. Scan reads only declared\n3838|non-auth roots, publishes observations and its Inventory Batch atomically, and\n3839|never claims that an active prefix is a cloning-safe boundary. Preview requires\n3840|the exact observation/head, defaults to public user/assistant roles, and\n3841|returns bounded redacted terminal-safe text. Raw native IDs and absolute paths\n3842|never leave the source except through an existing AX mutation authority.\n3843|\n3844|## 8. Provider and platform contracts\n3845|\n3846|### 8.1 Matrix notation\n3847|\n3848|Provider and platform matrices use:\n3849|\n3850|- <strong>A</strong>: available from documented or accepted evidence; runtime\n3851|  probe still MUST succeed;\n3852|- <strong>C</strong>: conditional and disabled until the named acceptance gate\n3853|  succeeds for the exact version/platform tuple;\n3854|- <strong>U</strong>: unsupported in v0.3.0 and disabled; and\n3855|- <strong>?</strong>: unknown and disabled because there is no sufficient\n3856|  contract or evidence.\n3857|\n3858|These labels are not aliases. In particular, unknown MUST NOT be rewritten as\n3859|unsupported, and conditional MUST NOT be advertised as available.\n3860|\n3861|### 8.2 Native-store contract matrix\n3862|\n3863|| Provider | Durable identity and native location | Resume/import surface | v0.3.0 materialization rule | Required exclusions and limits |\n3864|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3865|| Codex | Session UUID/name; known root <code>~/.codex/sessions</code>. Source absolute cwd is metadata. | <code>codex resume SESSION_ID</code>; current CLI also has <code>codex fork SESSION_ID</code>. | Adapter MUST stage only the closed session objects it has identified, compute the destination cwd mapping, validate discovery by explicit ID, and merge without replacing unrelated sessions. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until cross-host fixtures pass. | Authentication files, config secrets, MCP tokens, logs not required by the session, live processes, locks, SQLite/WAL/SHM, and runtime sockets. |\n3866|| Claude | Session UUID; known root <code>~/.claude/projects</code> with a provider-computed project key. | <code>claude --resume SESSION_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, and <code>--fork-session</code> when resuming. | Adapter MUST derive the destination project key from the logical workspace mapping, stage the closed session plus documented companion data, and validate explicit UUID resume. It MUST NOT copy the source project-directory key verbatim as identity. <code>portable_store</code> remains C. | OAuth/API credentials, settings secrets, MCP auth, live PTY state, PID/lock/socket files, caches, and unproven companion databases. |\n3867|| Gemini CLI | Session UUID scoped by logical project; documented root <code>~/.gemini/tmp/&lt;project-hash&gt;/chats</code>. | <code>gemini --resume UUID</code>, picker/index/latest, and <code>--session-file FILE</code>. | Adapter MUST compute the destination project hash, prefer the documented session-file import when compatible, stage atomically, then validate <code>--list-sessions</code> and explicit UUID resume. <code>portable_store</code> is C until schema/version and cross-platform fixtures pass. | Google credentials, API keys, settings secrets, trust state, runtime locks, cache-only files, and source path keys. |\n3868|| Muse | Session UUID; <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/muse/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/UUID</code>, defaulting below <code>~/.local/share</code>. | <code>muse resume UUID</code>, <code>--last</code>, picker, and <code>muse exec --session-id UUID</code>. Export exists; native import does not. | On probed macOS 0.1.0, a guarded adapter MAY stage the complete closed durable directory, omit transient files, validate with offline export, and resume explicitly. It MUST advertise <code>portable_store = false</code> because cron-aware, current-version, cross-host fidelity is not proven. | <code>~/.config/muse/auth.json</code>, keys, login state, <code>.session.lock</code>, sockets/tokens, live WAL/SHM/locks, updater/plugin caches. <code>cron.db</code> is durable but not safely portable; a session with active or non-empty scheduled work MUST fail materialization. |\n3869|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c625","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":365,"recorded_at":1780531400000725,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"c2010bc3-1267-4c2e-ba75-38fdaaeb742d"},"task_id":"c2010bc3-1267-4c2e-ba75-38fdaaeb742d","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"c2010bc3-1267-4c2e-ba75-38fdaaeb742d"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c627","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":366,"recorded_at":1780531400000727,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"call_id":"call_01a06f86e8507aa3a85342b3aa716d75","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2619 line(s) above)\n2620|## 7. Provider plugin protocol\n2621|\n2622|### 7.1 Discovery and trust\n2623|\n2624|Built-in support covers <code>codex</code>, <code>claude</code>,\n2625|<code>gemini</code>, <code>muse</code>, <code>antigravity</code>, and\n2626|<code>pi</code>. External provider executables are named\n2627|<code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code>, where <code>id</code> matches\n2628|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>.\n2629|\n2630|Candidate discovery order is:\n2631|\n2632|1. configured <code>providers.plugin_dirs</code> in listed order;\n2633|2. built-in adapters; then\n2634|3. <code>PATH</code>, only when <code>allow_path_plugins</code> is true.\n2635|\n2636|M0 establishes the versioned plugin wire contracts, internal implementation\n2637|interfaces, and a conformance harness. M0 MUST NOT advertise a public stable\n2638|plugin SDK. A stable public SDK remains deferred until both Codex and Claude\n2639|implementations validate that the boundary is sufficient without provider-\n2640|specific authority leakage or compatibility shims.\n2641|\n2642|The order does not establish precedence. If two candidates—including a built-in\n2643|and an executable—declare the same provider ID, discovery MUST fail with\n2644|<code>invalid_config</code> before either candidate is probed or executed.\n2645|Configuration schema 1.0.0 has no duplicate-selection override; the operator\n2646|must remove or rename one candidate. For each accepted external candidate, the\n2647|canonical absolute executable path and SHA-256 digest MUST be recorded at trust\n2648|time. Symlinks MUST be resolved before comparison, the target MUST be a regular\n2649|file owned by the operator or an administrator-approved identity, and a changed\n2650|path target or digest MUST require renewed trust. Plugins execute with the\n2651|operator's privileges and are inside the trusted-host boundary, but they MUST\n2652|receive only the minimum operation-specific inputs.\n2653|\n2654|### 7.2 Framing and lifecycle\n2655|\n2656|The provider protocol is line-delimited JSON over stdin/stdout with\n2657|<code>protocol = \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\"</code> and\n2658|<code>protocol_version = \"2.0.0\"</code>. Each line MUST be one complete UTF-8\n2659|JSON object no larger than 8 MiB. Stdout MUST contain protocol frames only;\n2660|human diagnostics go to stderr.\n2661|\n2662|<code>ax</code> starts one plugin process per operation. Requests are\n2663|single-flight in v2. After one response, <code>ax</code> closes stdin and the\n2664|plugin MUST exit. Exit 0 requires a successful response. A structured error\n2665|response SHOULD exit 0 because the protocol succeeded; a crash, invalid frame,\n2666|or missing response is a provider-host failure.\n2667|\n2668|Request envelope:\n2669|\n2670|~~~json\n2671|{\n2672|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2673|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2674|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2675|  \"operation\": \"doctor\",\n2676|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:05:00.000Z\",\n2677|  \"body\": {\n2678|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2679|    \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2680|    \"provider_executable\": \"/opt/local/bin/pi\",\n2681|    \"identity\": null\n2682|  }\n2683|}\n2684|~~~\n2685|\n2686|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2687|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n2688|<code>operation</code> from the Section 7.5 operation registry,\n2689|<code>deadline</code> timestamp, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>.\n2690|The deadline MUST be in the future when the host writes the frame.\n2691|\n2692|Success envelope:\n2693|\n2694|~~~json\n2695|{\n2696|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2697|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2698|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2699|  \"ok\": true,\n2700|  \"body\": {\n2701|    \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2702|    \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2703|    \"findings\": []\n2704|  }\n2705|}\n2706|~~~\n2707|\n2708|A success envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n2709|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>ok = true</code>,\n2710|and the operation-specific <code>body</code>. A failure envelope contains\n2711|exactly the first four members with <code>ok = false</code> plus\n2712|<code>error</code>, and MUST NOT contain <code>body</code>. Envelope and body\n2713|unknown members are protocol errors under major version 2.\n2714|\n2715|Failure envelope:\n2716|\n2717|~~~json\n2718|{\n2719|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n2720|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n2721|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-8e50-7f66-8f70-1234567890ab\",\n2722|  \"ok\": false,\n2723|  \"error\": {\n2724|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n2725|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2726|    \"code\": \"capability_unavailable\",\n2727|    \"message\": \"portable store is not available for this provider build\",\n2728|    \"exit_code\": 6,\n2729|    \"retryable\": false,\n2730|    \"details\": {}\n2731|  }\n2732|}\n2733|~~~\n2734|\n2735|Provider protocol <code>2.x</code> statically binds every failure envelope to\n2736|Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>. The error schema is not independently\n2737|negotiated on a provider invocation; a provider-protocol minor that needs a\n2738|different error schema must explicitly revise that binding. Section 15.1\n2739|defines supported-major, unsupported-major, and invalid-first-frame behavior.\n2740|\n2741|The host MUST terminate a plugin that exceeds its deadline and report\n2742|<code>provider_timeout</code>. It MUST redact environment and stderr before\n2743|logging.\n2744|\n2745|### 7.3 Provider Manifest\n2746|\n2747|The <code>manifest</code> operation requires an empty body and returns\n2748|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2749|\n2750|~~~json\n2751|{\n2752|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest\",\n2753|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2754|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2755|  \"display_name\": \"Pi\",\n2756|  \"plugin_version\": \"0.1.0\",\n2757|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.73.1 <0.74.0\",\n2758|  \"platforms\": [\"linux\", \"macos\", \"windows\", \"wsl2\"],\n2759|  \"operations\": [\n2760|    \"manifest\",\n2761|    \"probe\",\n2762|    \"launch\",\n2763|    \"identify-session\",\n2764|    \"quiesce\",\n2765|    \"native-store-plan\",\n2766|    \"capture\",\n2767|    \"materialize\",\n2768|    \"materialize-status\",\n2769|    \"materialize-commit\",\n2770|    \"materialize-rollback\",\n2771|    \"resume\",\n2772|    \"fork\",\n2773|    \"stop\",\n2774|    \"doctor\"\n2775|  ],\n2776|  \"capability_names\": [\n2777|    \"native_resume\",\n2778|    \"portable_store\",\n2779|    \"managed_pty\",\n2780|    \"appserver\",\n2781|    \"task_board_primary\",\n2782|    \"prompt_spawn\",\n2783|    \"native_goal_binding\"\n2784|  ]\n2785|}\n2786|~~~\n2787|\n2788|The manifest is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2789|<code>display_name</code> is 1–128 UTF-8 characters;\n2790|<code>plugin_version</code> is SemVer; <code>provider_version_range</code> is a\n2791|1–256 character provider-adapter constraint; <code>platforms</code> is a sorted,\n2792|unique non-empty subset of the four platform enums; <code>operations</code> is\n2793|the ordered registry shown in Section 7.5 with no duplicates; and\n2794|<code>capability_names</code> is the exact seven-name ordered registry shown.\n2795|The manifest declares possible surfaces, not runtime availability.\n2796|\n2797|### 7.4 Capability result\n2798|\n2799|The <code>probe</code> operation body contains platform, architecture,\n2800|provider executable path, and requested capability names. Its response MUST\n2801|identify the exact provider version and emit every known capability using\n2802|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-probe</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\n2803|\n2804|~~~json\n2805|{\n2806|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-probe\",\n2807|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2808|  \"provider_id\": \"pi\",\n2809|  \"provider_version\": \"0.73.1\",\n2810|  \"platform\": \"macos\",\n2811|  \"architecture\": \"arm64\",\n2812|  \"capabilities\": {\n2813|    \"native_resume\": {\n2814|      \"status\": \"available\",\n2815|      \"enabled\": true,\n2816|      \"evidence\": \"probed\",\n2817|      \"detail\": \"--session, --continue, and --resume are present\"\n2818|    },\n2819|    \"portable_store\": {\n2820|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2821|      \"enabled\": false,\n2822|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2823|      \"detail\": \"closed-store cross-host fixture has not passed\"\n2824|    },\n2825|    \"managed_pty\": {\n2826|      \"status\": \"conditional\",\n2827|      \"enabled\": false,\n2828|      \"evidence\": \"acceptance_required\",\n2829|      \"detail\": \"platform PTY interruption and flush gate has not passed\"\n2830|    },\n2831|    \"appserver\": {\n2832|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2833|      \"enabled\": false,\n2834|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2835|      \"detail\": \"Pi RPC is not claimed as the ax appserver capability\"\n2836|    },\n2837|    \"task_board_primary\": {\n2838|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2839|      \"enabled\": false,\n2840|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2841|      \"detail\": \"no reliable primary adapter is accepted\"\n2842|    },\n2843|    \"prompt_spawn\": {\n2844|      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n2845|      \"enabled\": false,\n2846|      \"evidence\": \"none\",\n2847|      \"detail\": \"not claimed for v0.3.0\"\n2848|    },\n2849|    \"native_goal_binding\": {\n2850|      \"status\": \"unsupported\",\n2851|      \"enabled\": false,\n2852|      \"evidence\": \"provider_contract\",\n2853|      \"detail\": \"no native task-board goal binding\"\n2854|    }\n2855|  },\n2856|  \"warnings\": []\n2857|}\n2858|~~~\n2859|\n2860|The probe object is closed and every displayed member is required.\n2861|<code>provider_version</code> is a 1–128 character exact version string,\n2862|architecture is <code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>, and\n2863|<code>capabilities</code> contains exactly the seven requested registry keys.\n2864|Each capability value contains exactly <code>status</code>,\n2865|<code>enabled</code>, <code>evidence</code>, and a 0–2,048 character\n2866|<code>detail</code>. <code>warnings</code> is a sorted, unique array of at most\n2867|1,024 strings of at most 2,048 characters each.\n2868|\n2869|Status is one of <code>available</code>, <code>conditional</code>,\n2870|<code>unsupported</code>, or <code>unknown</code>. Only\n2871|<code>available</code> MAY set <code>enabled</code> true. Evidence is one of\n2872|<code>documented</code>, <code>probed</code>, <code>accepted_test</code>,\n2873|<code>provider_contract</code>, <code>inferred</code>,\n2874|<code>acceptance_required</code>, or <code>none</code>.\n2875|\n2876|### 7.5 Required operations\n2877|\n2878|All plugins MUST implement every operation and return\n2879|<code>capability_unavailable</code> when the provider lacks the surface.\n2880|\n2881|Every request and success <code>body</code> is a closed object. The following\n2882|embedded types are part of provider protocol 2.0.0:\n2883|\n2884|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n2885|| --- | --- |\n2886|| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n2887|| <code>WorkspacePaths</code> | <code>map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]</code>; paths are destination-native, canonical, and contain no NUL |\n2888|| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\n2889|| <code>ProcessObservation</code> | <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>executable_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>candidate_store_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..256]</code>, <code>candidate_native_ids:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>; no PID is carried |\n2890|| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\n2891|| <code>SafeBoundaryProof</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean&#124;null</code>, <code>open_child_count:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handle_count:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique enum[0..5]</code> |\n2892|| <code>ValidationEvidence</code> | <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>status:passed&#124;skipped</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\n2893|| <code>NativeDiscoveryProof</code> | <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>discovered:boolean</code>, <code>discovery_root:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>backend_resolved:boolean</code> |\n2894|| <code>ProcessClosure</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n2895|| <code>DoctorFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>evidence:documented&#124;probed&#124;accepted_test&#124;provider_contract&#124;inferred&#124;acceptance_required&#124;none</code> |\n2896|| <code>ProviderStoreAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>access:capture_source&#124;materialize_destination</code> |\n2897|| <code>AuthorityTarget</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>relative_path:.&#124;path</code> |\n2898|| <code>ProviderCaptureItem</code> | <code>source_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>source_relative_path:path</code>, <code>manifest_path:path</code>, <code>kind:file&#124;directory</code>, <code>state_class:durable_payload&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>required:boolean</code> |\n2899|| <code>ProviderCapturePlan</code> | <code>capture_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_authorities:ProviderStoreAuthority[1..32]</code>, <code>items:ProviderCaptureItem[1..32768]</code>, <code>excluded_targets:AuthorityTarget[0..4096]</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, <code>snapshot_requires_closed_store:boolean</code> |\n2900|| <code>ObjectSink</code> | <code>root:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>create_mode:exclusive</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2901|| <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_objects</code>, <code>kind:provider_object_source</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>access:read_only</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2902|| <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>kind:provider_transaction</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:provider_transaction_v1</code>, <code>access:read_write</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids:sorted unique root-id[1..32]</code> |\n2903|| <code>ProviderTransactionEntry</code> | <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>provider_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>target_relative_path:path</code>, <code>expected_prior_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>prior_kind:absent&#124;file&#124;directory&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>backup_relative_path:path&#124;null</code>, <code>applied:boolean</code>, <code>restored:boolean</code> |\n2904|| <code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code> | <code>protocol:urn:ax:protocol:provider</code>, <code>protocol_version:2.0.0</code>, <code>document_kind:materialization_transaction</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>state:preparing&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;committed&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>entries:ProviderTransactionEntry[1..65536]</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp</code>, <code>terminal_at:timestamp&#124;null</code> |\n2905|| <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>state:unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code> |\n2906|\n2907|The <code>SafeBoundaryProof.blockers</code> enum is\n2908|<code>background_unproven</code>, <code>child_process_open</code>,\n2909|<code>database_handle_open</code>, <code>provider_busy</code>, or\n2910|<code>store_unstable</code>. A safe proof requires empty blockers,\n2911|<code>input_blocked</code>, <code>foreground_idle</code>,\n2912|<code>background_idle = true</code>, both counts zero, and non-null boundary and\n2913|store generation. <code>ValidationEvidence</code> arrays MUST be sorted by\n2914|<code>code</code> with no duplicate code. Opaque process handles are valid only\n2915|for the operation lifetime and MUST NOT be persisted or replicated.\n2916|\n2917|The <code>root-id</code> grammar is\n2918|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code>. Capture authorities are sorted by\n2919|<code>authority_id</code>, have <code>access = capture_source</code>, and are\n2920|unique. Capture items are sorted by <code>manifest_path</code>; each authority\n2921|reference MUST resolve, and\n2922|<code>root_path/source_relative_path</code> MUST remain under that exact root\n2923|after symlink/reparse-point resolution. Items MUST neither overlap nor traverse\n2924|through a symlink. Excluded targets are sorted by authority ID then relative\n2925|path and MUST reference the same authority set. <code>derived_cache</code> is\n2926|included only when Section 8 identifies it as required discovery metadata;\n2927|otherwise it must be excluded. Provider roots that contain credentials,\n2928|machine authentication, runtime sockets, locks, or live ax state MUST be\n2929|rejected even when a plugin names them. <code>ObjectSink.root</code> is a fresh owner-only directory\n2930|created by <code>ax</code>. Under <code>sha256_loose_v1</code>, a plugin writes\n2931|each complete blob with create-new semantics at\n2932|the exact Section 3.2 <code>digest_path_v1</code> relative path\n2933|<code>sha256/HH/REST</code> (two-hex shard, 62-hex leaf).\n2934|It MUST NOT create symlinks, hardlinks, devices, sockets, or any file not named\n2935|by its returned descriptors. The host independently hashes every sink file,\n2936|checks size/limits/exclusions, and only then imports it into the ax object\n2937|store. A plugin never receives the live object-store root.\n2938|\n2939|The destination host, not the peer and not the plugin, constructs both\n2940|materialization authorities. A <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority.root_path</code>\n2941|MUST equal\n2942|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-object-sources/&lt;materialization-id&gt;/&lt;provider-id&gt;</code>;\n2943|it is a fresh owner-only directory containing exactly the verified manifest\n2944|closure at the same <code>digest_path_v1</code> paths. The host makes every file read-only\n2945|before invoking the plugin. The authority's manifest IDs, byte/blob limits,\n2946|materialization ID, and provider ID MUST equal the selected checkpoint and\n2947|plan. An extra file, writable file, symlink, digest mismatch, or path supplied\n2948|by a remote request is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n2949|\n2950|A <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path</code> MUST equal\n2951|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-transactions/&lt;provider-id&gt;/&lt;transaction-id&gt;</code>.\n2952|It is a fresh owner-only directory, is disjoint from the object source and all\n2953|plan roots, and names exactly the materialization/provider/transaction/plan in\n2954|the authority. Its\n2955|<code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids</code> MUST equal the sorted set of\n2956|all <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority IDs used by plan operations. The\n2957|host MUST prove that the transaction root and every named provider-store root\n2958|are on the same filesystem/volume before the first plugin mutation. If one is\n2959|not, provider protocol 2.0.0 fails with <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>; it MUST\n2960|NOT fall back to an in-place cross-filesystem copy.\n2961|\n2962|The <code>provider_transaction_v1</code> layout contains only these durable\n2963|paths, plus one same-directory temporary file while atomically replacing\n2964|<code>transaction.json</code>:\n2965|\n2966|~~~text\n2967|transaction.json\n2968|staged/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2969|backups/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n2970|~~~\n2971|\n2972|<code>transaction.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the closed\n2973|<code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code>. Entries are sorted by sequence and\n2974|are exactly the provider-store operations in the plan. For a pre-existing\n2975|target, <code>backup_relative_path</code> is exactly\n2976|<code>backups/&lt;provider-authority-id&gt;/&lt;operation-sequence&gt;</code>; an absent\n2977|target requires <code>prior_kind = absent</code>, a null backup path, and a null\n2978|expected prior digest. Every other prior kind requires that exact non-null\n2979|backup path and a non-null expected prior digest. A prepared document has every\n2980|entry applied, no entry restored, a non-null rollback token, and non-null native\n2981|discovery. A committed document keeps the applied facts, sets the token to\n2982|null, removes every staged/backup payload from disk, and has non-null\n2983|discovery. A rolled-\n2984|back document has every pre-existing entry restored, every transaction-created\n2985|target removed, a null token, and discovery describing the restored\n2986|destination. The plugin MUST fsync a staged replacement and the\n2987|transaction document, atomically rename any predecessor into its backup, then\n2988|atomically rename the staged replacement into the exact target. Each document\n2989|transition is written to a fresh temporary regular file, fsynced, renamed over\n2990|<code>transaction.json</code>, and followed by a parent-directory fsync where\n2991|the platform supports it. Windows uses replace/write-through semantics with\n2992|equivalent user-only DACLs.\n2993|\n2994|<code>terminal_at</code> is null in <code>preparing</code>,\n2995|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n2996|<code>rolling_back</code> states and non-null in\n2997|<code>committed|rolled_back</code> states.\n2998|<code>updated_at</code> never precedes <code>created_at</code>, and terminal time\n2999|never precedes either. Timestamps are diagnostics; state, IDs, entry facts, and\n3000|filesystem verification decide recovery.\n3001|\n3002|Every transaction operation receives the same complete\n3003|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>. A fresh plugin process locates state\n3004|only through that authority, validates the path and\n3005|<code>transaction.json</code> IDs before acting, and MUST NOT use an ambient\n3006|transaction registry or search another root. A crash while\n3007|<code>preparing</code>, <code>committing</code>, or <code>rolling_back</code> is\n3008|reconciled from the entries to one exposed status before\n3009|<code>materialize-status</code> responds; an irreconcilable entry is\n3010|<code>integrity_failure</code> and retains the root for diagnosis. Prepared\n3011|documents store the rollback token under owner-only permissions so a later\n3012|process can reconstruct the current durable status; terminal documents set it\n3013|to null.\n3014|Commit removes all backups only after durable committed state; rollback\n3015|restores all predecessors before durable rolled-back state. The terminal\n3016|<code>transaction.json</code> receipt remains until the corresponding\n3017|Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\n3018|<code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> afterward. Object-source bytes and\n3019|backup/staged subtrees MAY then be removed; live or ambiguous roots MUST NOT be\n3020|garbage-collected.\n3021|\n3022|In <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code>, <code>unknown</code> requires null\n3023|plan/token/discovery; <code>prepared</code> requires all three non-null;\n3024|<code>committed</code> and <code>rolled_back</code> require a non-null plan and\n3025|discovery proof and a null rollback token. The discovery proof in a rolled-back\n3026|status describes the destination after rollback. An operation failure does not\n3027|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n3028|status request reports the last durable state. An unreadable or\n3029|integrity-invalid transaction MUST fail with <code>integrity_failure</code> and\n3030|MUST be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status object.\n3031|Every provider mutation request that carries <code>operation_id</code> uses the\n3032|single Provider protocol 2.0.0 idempotency key\n3033|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>. An\n3034|identical canonical mutation request MUST return a byte-identical result across\n3035|a fresh plugin process; any changed member is\n3036|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and MUST cause no new mutation. Observational\n3037|operations, including <code>materialize-status</code>, are evolving reads. They\n3038|use the provider envelope's fresh <code>request_id</code> only for correlation,\n3039|MUST NOT be stored as mutation receipts, and MUST return the durable state at\n3040|the read's reconciliation point even when an earlier identical read returned a\n3041|different phase. For <code>capture</code>, replay verifies/reuses only exact\n3042|digest-named files already present in the same Object Sink and re-emits the\n3043|same manifest/descriptors; an extra or changed file fails integrity. Provider\n3044|<code>fork</code> is side-effect-free and recomputes the same plan. The\n3045|materialize mutations use their durable transaction document as the receipt.\n3046|No operation relies on a searched ambient registry. Transaction IDs and\n3047|mutation operation IDs are caller-supplied and stable across retries. For one\n3048|provider materialization transaction, the <code>operation_id</code> is\n3049|transaction-wide across <code>materialize</code> and exactly one terminal\n3050|<code>materialize-commit</code> or <code>materialize-rollback</code>; a\n3051|<code>materialize-status</code> request omits it and locates the transaction only\n3052|through the caller-supplied materialization/transaction IDs and exact authority.\n3053|Reusing the mutation value across distinct operation tags does not alias their\n3054|recorded results. Within one provider ID,\n3055|an operation ID used by the materialize family identifies exactly one materialization transaction:\n3056|its <code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, plan ID, object\n3057|source, transaction authority, provider-store authorities, lease, activation,\n3058|rollback reason, and all remaining body members are immutable retry input for\n3059|their operation tag. Reusing <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> with any\n3060|different canonical body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>; the plugin MUST\n3061|return the first recorded result or failure and MUST NOT allocate, search, or\n3062|mutate another transaction root. A transaction or materialization ID already\n3063|bound to another operation ID is also <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. There\n3064|is no second tuple- or path-based idempotency key in provider protocol 2.0.0.\n3065|\n3066|The operation body registry is exact. A named schema object means the complete\n3067|validated object, not only its digest. Arrays of schema objects are sorted by\n3068|their canonical identity field and contain no duplicate identity:\n3069|\n3070|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3071|| --- | --- | --- |\n3072|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Provider Manifest object (Section 7.3) |\n3073|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\n3074|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3075|| <code>identify-session</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7, provider_id:provider-id, observation:ProcessObservation}</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak, matched_evidence:sorted unique native_id&#124;store_path&#124;provider_event&#124;backend_lookup[1..4]}</code> |\n3076|| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\n3077|| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, materialization_plan:Materialization Plan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], path_key_rewrites:map(UUIDv7,string[1..1024])[0..256]}</code> |\n3078|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, proof:SafeBoundaryProof, object_sink:ObjectSink, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_id:UUIDv7, manifest:Transfer Manifest, blob_descriptors:sorted unique Blob Descriptor[0..32768], written_blob_ids:sorted unique digest[0..32768], captured_store_generation:string[1..512], exclusions_applied:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code> |\n3079|| <code>materialize</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan:Materialization Plan, object_source:ProviderObjectSourceAuthority, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:prepared, created_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], merged_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], validations:ValidationEvidence[1..256], rollback_token:base64url-256+, native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof}</code> |\n3080|| <code>materialize-status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority}</code> | <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> |\n3081|| <code>materialize-commit</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, activation:dormant_validated&#124;owner_resumed, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:committed, backup_removed:boolean, committed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n3082|| <code>materialize-rollback</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:rolled_back, restored_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], removed_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], native_discovery_absent:boolean}</code> |\n3083|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3084|| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\n3085|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, mode:graceful&#124;force, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{closure:ProcessClosure}</code> |\n3086|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, identity:Provider Identity Record&#124;null}</code> | <code>{provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128]&#124;null, findings:DoctorFinding[0..1024]}</code> |\n3087|\n3088|For <code>launch</code>, the profile and launch plan MUST exactly equal their\n3089|Session Record values. Provider <code>fork</code> is a planning call: it MUST\n3090|NOT write a provider store, allocate an active backend conversation, or start a\n3091|process. Its operation ID is the Session Record's\n3092|<code>fork_provenance.operation_id</code>; an identical retry returns the same\n3093|plan and any changed body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. The new record\n3094|MUST contain Fork Provenance matching the source/checkpoint and operation, and\n3095|a successful result requires <code>provenance_verified = true</code> and MUST\n3096|NOT describe a blank session. <code>native_fork</code> requires\n3097|<code>requires_provider_materialization = false</code> and MAY have a planned\n3098|native ID when the provider allocates it only at process start.\n3099|<code>supported_import</code> requires\n3100|<code>requires_provider_materialization = true</code>; the coordinator then\n3101|calls <code>native-store-plan phase=materialize</code> with\n3102|<code>mode=fork</code> and includes the validated provider plan in the\n3103|destination materialization transaction. In both variants, a new Provider\n3104|Identity Record is authoritative only after native discovery following the\n3105|prepared transaction; the planned ID is an expectation, not an identity\n3106|record.\n3107|\n3108|<code>launch</code>, <code>resume</code>, and <code>fork</code> return plans; the\n3109|trusted terminal backend performs process creation. Plugins MUST NOT return\n3110|secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\n3111|advertised portable-store tuple and MUST separate durable includes,\n3112|machine-local excludes, path-key rewrites, quiescence preconditions, and\n3113|validation steps. Its two request and result variants are closed and disjoint:\n3114|a capture request has no destination platform, destination host, destination\n3115|workspace map, or source manifest; a materialize request has no source\n3116|workspace map. Capture therefore works for the first local checkpoint without\n3117|inventing a destination peer or a source-as-destination sentinel.\n3118|\n3119|The capture result's authorities are the complete provider source-root\n3120|authority for that capture. A materialize plan MUST contain at least one\n3121|Section 10.5 <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority with\n3122|<code>prepared_for_host_id = destination_host_id</code>. Every such authority\n3123|MUST have the same provider/platform as the request, resolve to a\n3124|destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\n3125|disjoint from ax data/state/cache/runtime roots, task-board staging,\n3126|workspaces, and credential/authentication roots unless an exact child path is\n3127|the provider's documented durable store. A path-key rewrite is keyed by logical\n3128|workspace ID and contains destination-derived non-secret cache-key data, never\n3129|a source absolute path. An unavailable surface returns the common failure\n3130|envelope, not a success body with a null required plan.\n3131|\n3132|The following source-only first-checkpoint body and result are the normative\n3133|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-POS</code> fixture. Their absence of every\n3134|destination member is intentional:\n3135|\n3136|~~~json\n3137|{\n3138|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3139|  \"identity\": {\n3140|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3141|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3142|    \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3143|    \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3144|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3145|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3146|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3147|    \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3148|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3149|    \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3150|    \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3151|    \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3152|    \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3153|    \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3154|    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3155|    \"extensions\": {}\n3156|  },\n3157|  \"source_platform\": \"macos\",\n3158|  \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3159|  \"source_workspace_paths\": {\n3160|    \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/payments-api\"\n3161|  },\n3162|  \"lease\": {\n3163|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3164|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n3165|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3166|  }\n3167|}\n3168|~~~\n3169|\n3170|~~~json\n3171|{\n3172|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3173|  \"capture_plan\": {\n3174|    \"capture_id\": \"0198f4c8-0790-72aa-8374-3234567890ab\",\n3175|    \"source_authorities\": [\n3176|      {\n3177|        \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3178|        \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3179|        \"platform\": \"macos\",\n3180|        \"root_path\": \"/Users/iv/.codex/sessions\",\n3181|        \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n3182|        \"access\": \"capture_source\"\n3183|      }\n3184|    ],\n3185|    \"items\": [\n3186|      {\n3187|        \"source_authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3188|        \"source_relative_path\": \"2026/08/19/rollout-11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555.jsonl\",\n3189|        \"manifest_path\": \"session/rollout.jsonl\",\n3190|        \"kind\": \"file\",\n3191|        \"state_class\": \"durable_payload\",\n3192|        \"required\": true\n3193|      }\n3194|    ],\n3195|    \"excluded_targets\": [],\n3196|    \"store_generation\": \"closed:11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555:1\",\n3197|    \"snapshot_requires_closed_store\": true\n3198|  },\n3199|  \"include_classes\": [\"durable_payload\"],\n3200|  \"exclude_classes\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"]\n3201|}\n3202|~~~\n3203|\n3204|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N1</code> adds\n3205|<code>destination_platform</code> to the capture body and MUST fail with\n3206|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\n3207|the item authority to an undeclared ID and MUST fail before any provider byte\n3208|is read. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N3</code> makes the source authority equal\n3209|the credential root and MUST fail with <code>secret_policy_violation</code>.\n3210|\n3211|<code>capture</code> is the only provider operation that may emit provider\n3212|payload bytes. It requires <code>proof.safe = true</code>, equal proof/plan store\n3213|generation, and the current lease. Its manifest MUST have\n3214|<code>kind = provider</code>, the session as subject, and exactly the returned\n3215|descriptor/blob closure. The host MUST reject an extra sink file, missing\n3216|required item, descriptor mismatch, excluded class/path, generation change, or\n3217|secret-policy violation and MUST discard the isolated sink without importing\n3218|it. The plugin MUST NOT write a live ax store, live SQLite index, credential\n3219|root, or destination native store during capture.\n3220|\n3221|Provider materialization is a recoverable two-decision transaction.\n3222|<code>materialize</code> applies the exact plan while retaining every replaced\n3223|destination byte under the authorized transaction layout and returns\n3224|<code>state = prepared</code>; it MUST NOT delete its backup. While prepared,\n3225|the host validates exact native discovery and either keeps the replica dormant\n3226|or starts the winning owner. It then calls <code>materialize-commit</code> to\n3227|discard the backup, or <code>materialize-rollback</code> to restore it. Commit\n3228|requires <code>backup_removed = true</code>; rollback requires the native\n3229|identity introduced by the transaction to be absent afterward unless it was a\n3230|pre-existing backend identity. A rollback token is machine-local recovery\n3231|authority, MUST be at least 256 random bits, MUST be stored only in the\n3232|owner-only Materialization Journal and prepared Provider Transaction Document,\n3233|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n3234|\n3235|The provider plugin MUST execute only plan operations whose authority has\n3236|<code>kind = provider_store</code> and whose <code>provider_id</code> equals the\n3237|plugin manifest ID. The ax host executes workspace and task-board operations;\n3238|it MUST reject a plugin response that reports any created or merged path\n3239|outside the selected provider-store authorities. The plugin resolves each\n3240|reported absolute path from that authority's root plus the operation's\n3241|relative target, rechecks the predecessor immediately before mutation, and\n3242|uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\n3243|transaction containing disjoint authority-specific executors, not a grant for\n3244|the provider plugin to mutate the workspace.\n3245|\n3246|The three mutation operations use the same parent <code>operation_id</code>,\n3247|<code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, and byte-identical\n3248|transaction authority. The sole mutation idempotency key remains\n3249|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>; the materialization and transaction IDs\n3250|are immutable non-key inputs. Each mutation tag therefore has a distinct key\n3251|while all phases locate the same authority. A retry of one mutation name MUST\n3252|use byte-identical canonical arguments. <code>materialize-status</code> omits\n3253|<code>operation_id</code>; it is the required evolving lost-response recovery\n3254|read and uses the envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation. A status\n3255|read MUST reconcile and return the current durable state, so a read that once\n3256|returned <code>prepared</code> may later return <code>committed</code> or\n3257|<code>rolled_back</code>. An unknown transaction MUST return state\n3258|<code>unknown</code>; the host MUST NOT infer success. A prepared transaction\n3259|survives plugin/host restart until explicit commit or rollback. A plugin that\n3260|cannot provide this prepare/status/commit/rollback behavior MUST advertise\n3261|<code>portable_store</code> disabled.\n3262|\n3263|Normative prepared result body:\n3264|\n3265|~~~json\n3266|{\n3267|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3268|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n3269|  \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n3270|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n3271|  \"state\": \"prepared\",\n3272|  \"created_paths\": [\"/srv/provider/sessions/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"],\n3273|  \"merged_paths\": [],\n3274|  \"validations\": [\n3275|    {\"code\":\"native_discovery\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"detail\":\"exact session identity resolved\"}\n3276|  ],\n3277|  \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n3278|  \"native_discovery\": {\n3279|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3280|    \"discovered\": true,\n3281|    \"discovery_root\": \"/srv/provider/sessions\",\n3282|    \"backend_resolved\": false\n3283|  }\n3284|}\n3285|~~~\n3286|\n3287|The normative transaction cases are:\n3288|\n3289|| Fixture | Calls | Required terminal state |\n3290|| --- | --- | --- |\n3291|| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\n3292|| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\n3293|| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\n3294|| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\n3295|| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\n3296|| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\n3297|| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\n3298|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\n3299|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\n3300|\n3301|Changing a plan, object-source authority, or transaction authority on a repeated\n3302|<code>materialize</code>, changing activation/lease on a repeated commit, or\n3303|changing rollback reason/token on a repeated rollback while reusing the same\n3304|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code> key is the normative negative\n3305|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\n3306|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3307|\n3308|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\n3309|same <code>(materialize, operation_id)</code> while changing only\n3310|<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\n3311|<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\n3312|one authority root. Each MUST return <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, leave the\n3313|original transaction document/root byte-identical, and create no second root.\n3314|\n3315|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3316|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3317|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3318|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3319|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3320|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3321|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3322|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3323|\n3324|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3325|\n3326|~~~json\n3327|{\n3328|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3329|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3330|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3331|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3332|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3333|  \"body\": {\n3334|    \"identity\": {\n3335|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3336|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3337|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3338|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3339|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3340|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3341|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3342|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3343|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3344|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3345|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3346|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3347|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3348|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3349|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3350|      \"extensions\": {}\n3351|    },\n3352|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3353|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3354|    },\n3355|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3356|    \"terminal\": {\n3357|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3358|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3359|      \"interactive\": true,\n3360|      \"columns\": 120,\n3361|      \"rows\": 40\n3362|    },\n3363|    \"lease\": {\n3364|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3365|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3366|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3367|    }\n3368|  }\n3369|}\n3370|~~~\n3371|\n3372|~~~json\n3373|{\n3374|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3375|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3376|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3377|  \"ok\": true,\n3378|  \"body\": {\n3379|    \"argv\": [\n3380|      \"codex\",\n3381|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3382|      \"resume\",\n3383|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3384|    ],\n3385|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3386|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3387|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3388|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3389|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3390|    \"extensions\": {}\n3391|  }\n3392|}\n3393|~~~\n3394|\n3395|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3396|\n3397|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3398|\n3399|- provider ID and exact version;\n3400|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3401|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3402|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3403|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3404|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3405|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3406|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3407|\n3408|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3409|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3410|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3411|request.\n3412|\n3413|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3414|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3415|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3416|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3417|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3418|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3419|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3420|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3421|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3422|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3423|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3424|\n3425|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3426|\n3427|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3428|\n3429|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3430|| --- | --- |\n3431|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3432|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3433|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3434|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3435|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3436|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3437|\n3438|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3439|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3440|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3441|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3442|probe accepts them.\n3443|\n3444|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3445|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3446|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3447|confirmation controls still apply.\n3448|\n3449|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3450|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3451|\n3452|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3453|\n3454|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3455|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3456|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3457|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3458|\n3459|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3460|| --- | --- |\n3461|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3462|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3463|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3464|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3465|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3466|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3467|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3468|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3469|\n3470|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3471|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3472|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3473|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3474|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3475|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3476|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3477|\n3478|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3479|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3480|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3481|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3482|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3483|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3484|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3485|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3486|\n3487|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3488|\n3489|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3490|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3491|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3492|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3493|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3494|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3495|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3496|\n3497|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3498|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3499|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3500|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3501|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3502|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3503|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3504|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3505|\n3506|The closed operation registry is:\n3507|\n3508|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3509|| --- | --- |\n3510|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3511|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3512|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3513|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3514|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3515|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3516|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3517|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3518|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3519|\n3520|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3521|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3522|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3523|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3524|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3525|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3526|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3527|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3528|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3529|every candidate object.\n3530|\n3531|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3532|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3533|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3534|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3535|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3536|\n3537|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3538|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3539|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3540|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3541|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3542|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3543|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3544|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3545|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3546|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3547|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3548|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3549|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3550|  never paths.\n3551|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3552|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3553|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3554|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3555|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3556|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3557|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3558|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3559|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3560|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3561|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3562|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3563|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3564|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3565|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3566|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3567|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3568|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3569|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3570|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3571|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3572|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3573|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3574|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3575|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3576|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3577|\n3578|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3579|\n3580|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3581|| --- | --- | --- |\n3582|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3583|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3584|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3585|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3586|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3587|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3588|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3589|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3590|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3591|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3592|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3593|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3594|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3595|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3596|\n3597|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3598|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3599|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3600|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3601|and never fallback permission.\n3602|\n3603|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3604|\n3605|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3606|| --- | --- |\n3607|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3608|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3609|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3610|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3611|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3612|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3613|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3614|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3615|\n3616|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3617|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3618|\n3619|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3620|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3621|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3622|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3623|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3624|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3625|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3626|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3627|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3628|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3629|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3630|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3631|never contains executable provenance.\n3632|\n3633|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3634|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3635|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3636|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3637|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3638|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3639|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3640|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3641|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3642|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3643|\n3644|Each capability value contains exactly\n3645|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3646|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3647|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3648|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3649|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3650|\n3651|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3652|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3653|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3654|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3655|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3656|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3657|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3658|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3659|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3660|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3661|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3662|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3663|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3664|\n3665|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3666|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3667|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3668|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3669|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3670|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3671|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3672|write.\n3673|\n3674|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3675|\n3676|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3677|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3678|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3679|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3680|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3681|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3682|\n3683|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3684|\n3685|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3686|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3687|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3688|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3689|\n3690|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3691|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3692|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3693|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3694|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3695|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3696|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3697|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3698|shared.\n3699|\n3700|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3701|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3702|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3703|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3704|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3705|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3706|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3707|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3708|uses an empty body.\n3709|\n3710|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3711|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3712|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3713|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3714|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3715|Error 1.2 has\n3716|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n3717|<code>retryable=false</code>, and then exit with status 6. Only that complete\n3718|response-plus-exit tuple authorizes the caller to launch a fresh process for\n3719|the next lower locally supported major. The response is negotiation evidence,\n3720|not trusted manifest data and not an ordinary retryable operation failure.\n3721|\n3722|Success requires one well-framed success response with every echo exact, a\n3723|complete schema-valid manifest whose <code>supported_protocol_versions</code>\n3724|contains the exact selected version, and process exit 0. A wrong or missing\n3725|echo, malformed/partial/extra frame, invalid UTF-8/JSON/schema, timeout,\n3726|signal, nonmatching exit status, authentication/allowlist failure, integrity\n3727|failure, or any error other than the exact downgrade tuple is terminal and\n3728|MUST NOT cause a lower-major attempt. The caller MUST NOT reinterpret a frame,\n3729|manifest, platform token, request body, or error from one major as another.\n3730|If every locally supported major returns the exact downgrade tuple, the caller\n3731|terminates with its own Structured Error 1.2\n3732|<code>incompatible_protocol</code>, exit 6, and no trusted manifest or partial\n3733|result. These rules select v2 directly, permit v2-to-v1 fallback, support a\n3734|v1-only caller/peer, and terminate deterministically when no major is common.\n3735|\n3736|Transport is one request and one response as line-delimited JSON over\n3737|authenticated local stdio or allowlisted AX SSH. One line is at most 8 MiB.\n3738|The request envelope contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n3739|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>protocol</code>,\n3740|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3741|<code>operation</code>, <code>deadline_ms:uint53[1..3600000]</code>, and the\n3742|closed operation <code>body</code>. The response echoes protocol/version,\n3743|request/operation. A success response contains exactly the common envelope\n3744|members, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>, with no <code>error</code>\n3745|member. A failure response contains exactly the common envelope members,\n3746|<code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.2.0 in <code>error</code>, with no\n3747|<code>body</code> member. Unknown fields, both or neither branch members, invalid\n3748|UTF-8/JSON, multiple frames, wrong echo, oversize, timeout, or exit without one\n3749|valid response fail with no partial trusted data. Stdout is protocol-only;\n3750|redacted diagnostics use stderr.\n3751|\n3752|The Directory Node Manifest contains exactly schema/version,\n3753|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3754|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3755|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3756|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3757|<code>supported_protocol_versions:sorted unique SemVer[1..16]</code>,\n3758|<code>operations:sorted unique DirectoryNodeOperation[11]</code>,\n3759|<code>schemas:sorted unique ContractAssertion[15..64]</code>,\n3760|<code>environment_tuple_registry_id:digest</code>,\n3761|<code>capabilities:map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult)[8]</code>,\n3762|<code>redaction_policy_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n3763|<code>enrichment_profile_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>,\n3764|<code>limits:DirectoryNodeLimits</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. The three\n3765|façade executable/module bindings and tuple declarations MUST agree; a\n3766|contradiction is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3767|\n3768|<code>CapabilityResult</code> contains exactly\n3769|<code>status:available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code>,\n3770|<code>reason_code:string[1..128]|null</code>,\n3771|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>,\n3772|<code>observed_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Available has a\n3773|null reason; every other status requires one. <code>DirectoryNodeLimits</code>\n3774|contains exactly <code>max_frame_bytes:uint53[1..8388608]</code>,\n3775|<code>max_scan_instances:uint53[1..65536]</code>,\n3776|<code>max_inventory_take:uint53[1..1000]</code>,\n3777|<code>max_excerpt_count:uint53[0..20]</code>,\n3778|<code>max_excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096]</code>,\n3779|<code>max_enrichment_events:uint53[1..5000]</code>,\n3780|<code>max_enrichment_bytes:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n3781|<code>extensions</code>. Both nested objects are closed except for their listed\n3782|reverse-DNS extension maps.\n3783|\n3784|The exact operation registry and bodies are:\n3785|\n3786|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body | Mutation |\n3787|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3788|| <code>manifest</code> | empty object | complete Directory Node Manifest | none |\n3789|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,architecture:amd64\\|arm64,requested_environment_ids:sorted unique environment-id[0..64],requested_capabilities:sorted unique directory-capability[0..8],extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,node_build:DirectoryNodeBuild,policy_digest:digest,environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..256],findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code> | none |\n3790|| <code>scan</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],prior_batch_id:digest|null,cursor:string[1..4096]|null,max_instances:uint53[1..65536],extensions}</code> | <code>{batch:InventoryBatch,environment_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],native_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,extensions}</code> | directory records only |\n3791|| <code>inventory</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],fields:sorted unique observation-field[1..32],after:string[1..4096]|null,take:uint53[1..1000],extensions}</code> | <code>{observations:NativeSessionObservation[0..1000],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code> | none |\n3792|| <code>preview</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,roles:sorted unique user\\|assistant[1..2],excerpt_count:uint53[0..20],excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096],redaction_policy_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,instance_id:digest,observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,excerpts:PreviewExcerpt[0..20],truncated:boolean,redaction_summary:RedactionSummary,freshness:DirectoryFreshness,extensions}</code> | none |\n3793|| <code>enrichment-plan</code> | <code>{request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{accepted:boolean,expected_input_events:uint53,expected_input_bytes:uint53,expected_model_calls:uint53,disclosure_classes:sorted unique string[0..64],blockers:sorted unique string[0..128],extensions}</code> | none |\n3794|| <code>enrichment-run</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | annotation/job records only |\n3795|| <code>enrichment-status</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,receipt_chain_ids:digest[1..4096],produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | none |\n3796|| <code>continuation-inspect</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,management_binding:ManagementBinding,safe_boundary_status:proven\\|unproven\\|not_required,runtime_status:RuntimeExpectation,warnings:sorted unique string[0..256],extensions}</code> | none |\n3797|| <code>runtime-observe</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{runtime:RuntimeExpectation,extensions}</code> | none |\n3798|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256],include_conformance_age:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{healthy:boolean,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],environment_capabilities:map(digest,map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult))[0..256],cloning_contracts:sorted unique ContractAssertion[0..64],extensions}</code> | none |\n3799|\n3800|Each displayed body is closed; its member types, ordering, and limits are the\n3801|registered Section 10.8 schemas and manifest bounds. The <code>probe</code> row\n3802|shown above is the Request 2.0.0 form; Request 1.0.0 differs only in its closed\n3803|legacy platform vocabulary recorded in the major-binding table. The capability\n3804|registry is exactly <code>directory_discovery</code>,\n3805|<code>directory_incremental_scan</code>, <code>directory_head_digest</code>,\n3806|<code>directory_tail_preview</code>, <code>native_title_read</code>,\n3807|<code>native_runtime_observation</code>,\n3808|<code>existing_session_adoption</code>, and <code>native_resume</code>.\n3809|The closed <code>observation-field</code> registry is exactly\n3810|<code>identity</code>, <code>management</code>, <code>head</code>,\n3811|<code>state</code>, <code>workspace</code>, <code>title</code>,\n3812|<code>counts</code>, <code>preview_status</code>, <code>warnings</code>, and\n3813|<code>timestamps</code>. <code>PreviewExcerpt</code> contains exactly\n3814|<code>role:user|assistant</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n3815|<code>text:string[0..4096]</code>, <code>source_event_id:digest</code>,\n3816|<code>truncated:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3817|<code>ManagementBinding</code> contains exactly\n3818|<code>state:managed|unmanaged|conflicted</code>,\n3819|<code>session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n3820|<code>provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n3821|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n3822|<code>extensions</code>; both IDs and non-empty evidence are required exactly\n3823|for managed, both IDs are null for unmanaged, and conflicted retains all\n3824|evidence without choosing a winner. These nested objects are closed except for\n3825|their listed extension maps. <code>DirectoryNodeBuild</code> contains exactly\n3826|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3827|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3828|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3829|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3830|<code>extensions</code>; every value equals the current manifest.\n3831|Discovery may degrade for an unknown source tuple only when stable identity and\n3832|bounds remain safe; head/preview/resume/adoption/write/launch fail closed.\n3833|\n3834|<code>scan</code> and <code>enrichment-run</code> use\n3835|<code>(operation,operation_id)</code> idempotency. Repeating the same canonical\n3836|body returns the prior durable result; a changed body is\n3837|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> without new records. Scan reads only declared\n3838|non-auth roots, publishes observations and its Inventory Batch atomically, and\n3839|never claims that an active prefix is a cloning-safe boundary. Preview requires\n3840|the exact observation/head, defaults to public user/assistant roles, and\n3841|returns bounded redacted terminal-safe text. Raw native IDs and absolute paths\n3842|never leave the source except through an existing AX mutation authority.\n3843|\n3844|## 8. Provider and platform contracts\n3845|\n3846|### 8.1 Matrix notation\n3847|\n3848|Provider and platform matrices use:\n3849|\n3850|- <strong>A</strong>: available from documented or accepted evidence; runtime\n3851|  probe still MUST succeed;\n3852|- <strong>C</strong>: conditional and disabled until the named acceptance gate\n3853|  succeeds for the exact version/platform tuple;\n3854|- <strong>U</strong>: unsupported in v0.3.0 and disabled; and\n3855|- <strong>?</strong>: unknown and disabled because there is no sufficient\n3856|  contract or evidence.\n3857|\n3858|These labels are not aliases. In particular, unknown MUST NOT be rewritten as\n3859|unsupported, and conditional MUST NOT be advertised as available.\n3860|\n3861|### 8.2 Native-store contract matrix\n3862|\n3863|| Provider | Durable identity and native location | Resume/import surface | v0.3.0 materialization rule | Required exclusions and limits |\n3864|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3865|| Codex | Session UUID/name; known root <code>~/.codex/sessions</code>. Source absolute cwd is metadata. | <code>codex resume SESSION_ID</code>; current CLI also has <code>codex fork SESSION_ID</code>. | Adapter MUST stage only the closed session objects it has identified, compute the destination cwd mapping, validate discovery by explicit ID, and merge without replacing unrelated sessions. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until cross-host fixtures pass. | Authentication files, config secrets, MCP tokens, logs not required by the session, live processes, locks, SQLite/WAL/SHM, and runtime sockets. |\n3866|| Claude | Session UUID; known root <code>~/.claude/projects</code> with a provider-computed project key. | <code>claude --resume SESSION_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, and <code>--fork-session</code> when resuming. | Adapter MUST derive the destination project key from the logical workspace mapping, stage the closed session plus documented companion data, and validate explicit UUID resume. It MUST NOT copy the source project-directory key verbatim as identity. <code>portable_store</code> remains C. | OAuth/API credentials, settings secrets, MCP auth, live PTY state, PID/lock/socket files, caches, and unproven companion databases. |\n3867|| Gemini CLI | Session UUID scoped by logical project; documented root <code>~/.gemini/tmp/&lt;project-hash&gt;/chats</code>. | <code>gemini --resume UUID</code>, picker/index/latest, and <code>--session-file FILE</code>. | Adapter MUST compute the destination project hash, prefer the documented session-file import when compatible, stage atomically, then validate <code>--list-sessions</code> and explicit UUID resume. <code>portable_store</code> is C until schema/version and cross-platform fixtures pass. | Google credentials, API keys, settings secrets, trust state, runtime locks, cache-only files, and source path keys. |\n3868|| Muse | Session UUID; <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/muse/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/UUID</code>, defaulting below <code>~/.local/share</code>. | <code>muse resume UUID</code>, <code>--last</code>, picker, and <code>muse exec --session-id UUID</code>. Export exists; native import does not. | On probed macOS 0.1.0, a guarded adapter MAY stage the complete closed durable directory, omit transient files, validate with offline export, and resume explicitly. It MUST advertise <code>portable_store = false</code> because cron-aware, current-version, cross-host fidelity is not proven. | <code>~/.config/muse/auth.json</code>, keys, login state, <code>.session.lock</code>, sockets/tokens, live WAL/SHM/locks, updater/plugin caches. <code>cron.db</code> is durable but not safely portable; a session with active or non-empty scheduled work MUST fail materialization. |\n3869|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
