{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c647","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":382,"recorded_at":1780531400000759,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"709b66b4-5845-4833-bf83-46ebdc064c42"},"task_id":"709b66b4-5845-4833-bf83-46ebdc064c42","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"709b66b4-5845-4833-bf83-46ebdc064c42","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3868 line(s) above)\n3869|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n3870|| Pi | Session UUID/file; <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> or the configured <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR</code>/<code>--session-dir</code>. | <code>--session PATH_OR_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, <code>--resume</code>, <code>--fork</code>. | Adapter MUST snapshot a closed JSONL session and required non-secret companion data, map the destination cwd/session directory, validate the session ID, and resume explicitly. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until versioned cross-host fixtures pass. | <code>auth.json</code>, provider keys/tokens, extension secrets, live process state, locks, sockets, and caches. Pi 0.73.1 has no YOLO flag. |\n3871|| Qwen through task-board | The task-board bundle and manager-owned provider identity; there is no v0.2.1 direct claim and no v0.3.0 direct <code>ax-provider-qwen</code> claim. | Official task-board open/adopt only. | U for direct native materialization. A task-board prompt-mode bundle follows Section 9 and remains opaque. | All private manager/provider state except bytes included by the official bundle exporter. |\n3872|| Future plugin | Declared by plugin and exact probe. | Declared by plugin. | Every cell starts ?/disabled. Promotion requires Section 19 acceptance evidence. | Common exclusions plus plugin-specific exclusions. |\n3873|\n3874|Muse and Antigravity rows above are normative uses of the accepted\n3875|<code>TASK-260819-1ecd6x</code> evidence. The controlled Muse placement probe\n3876|does not create a supported import contract. Antigravity backend resolution is\n3877|native resume but not portable storage.\n3878|\n3879|### 8.3 Capability matrix\n3880|\n3881|| Provider | <code>native_resume</code> | <code>portable_store</code> | <code>managed_pty</code> | <code>appserver</code> | <code>task_board_primary</code> | <code>prompt_spawn</code> | <code>native_goal_binding</code> |\n3882|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3883|| Codex | A | C | C | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3884|| Claude | A | C | C | U for direct adapter | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3885|| Gemini CLI | A | C | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3886|| Muse | C by platform/version | U | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3887|| Antigravity CLI | C: backend realm required | U | C | ? | U | ? | U |\n3888|| Pi | A | C | C | U; Pi RPC is not claimed as this capability | ? | ? | U |\n3889|| Qwen through task-board | U direct | U direct | U direct | U direct | U | A through task-board | U |\n3890|| Future plugin | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? |\n3891|\n3892|For Codex and Claude, task-board owns app-server/thread or PTY mechanics,\n3893|reattach, resume, and goal binding. The direct Claude adapter therefore does\n3894|not advertise <code>appserver</code>. The task-board capability plane and\n3895|direct-provider capability plane MUST NOT be conflated.\n3896|\n3897|### 8.4 Provider/platform matrix\n3898|\n3899|Each cell is <code>native resume / cross-host materialization / managed\n3900|terminal</code>. Task-board-only behavior is stated separately.\n3901|\n3902|| Provider/platform | Status | Normative limit |\n3903|| --- | --- | --- |\n3904|| Codex / macOS | A / C / C | Resume and unrestricted flag are documented; portable store and PTY flush require adapter fixtures. |\n3905|| Codex / Linux | A / C / C | Same; exact distribution and filesystem fixture required. |\n3906|| Codex / WSL2 | A / C / C | Treat as Linux with a Linux store. Repositories SHOULD live below the WSL home, not a Windows-mounted path. |\n3907|| Codex / native Windows | A / C / C | Native CLI is documented. ConPTY, Windows store discovery, file locking, and sandbox mode MUST pass. Windows 11 is the release baseline; Windows 10 is best effort and requires ConPTY. |\n3908|| Claude / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 2.1.229 help confirms UUID resume and unrestricted flag; store transfer remains gated. |\n3909|| Claude / Linux | A / C / C | Provider family documented; distro/PTTY fixture required. |\n3910|| Claude / WSL2 | A / C / C | WSL is provider-documented; use Linux store and path rules. |\n3911|| Claude / native Windows | C / C / C | Windows 10+ with WSL or Git for Windows is documented, but native PowerShell/ConPTY and native store materialization require acceptance. |\n3912|| Gemini / macOS | A / C / C | Official session root, UUID resume, and session-file surface documented. |\n3913|| Gemini / Linux | A / C / C | Ubuntu 20.04+ documented; other distributions conditional. |\n3914|| Gemini / WSL2 | C / C / C | Linux inference; mounted-filesystem, auth, signal, and path-hash tests required. |\n3915|| Gemini / native Windows | A / C / C | Windows 11 24H2+ documented; PowerShell/ConPTY and path-hash tests required. |\n3916|| Muse / macOS arm64 | A for probed 0.1.0 / U / C | Narrow resume probe accepted; current 0.2.1 and full idle/cron fidelity remain unverified. |\n3917|| Muse / macOS amd64 | C / U / C | Artifact/contract exists; not executed. |\n3918|| Muse / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Official launcher artifacts; not executed. |\n3919|| Muse / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux-path inference only. |\n3920|| Muse / native Windows | ? / U / ? | 0.2.1 artifacts exist, but official launcher and persistence contract do not establish support. |\n3921|| Antigravity / macOS amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Resume works only when the authenticated backend realm resolves the UUID; <code>Stop.fullyIdle</code> is documented. |\n3922|| Antigravity / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; keyring/DBus and PTY tests required. |\n3923|| Antigravity / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux inference only; auth, path, signal, and locking tests required. |\n3924|| Antigravity / native Windows amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; ConPTY, data-root expansion, and file-lock tests required. |\n3925|| Pi / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 0.73.1 help verifies session surfaces and default full tool set. |\n3926|| Pi / Linux | C / C / C | Cross-platform Node/package behavior is plausible but exact 0.73.1 acceptance is required. |\n3927|| Pi / WSL2 | C / C / C | Treat as Linux only after path/signal/auth tests. |\n3928|| Pi / native Windows | C / C / C | Provider platform notes exist; exact 0.73.1 store, shell, and ConPTY behavior is unverified. |\n3929|| Qwen task-board prompt mode / any target platform | U direct; A only where task-board probe reports <code>prompt_spawn</code> | No direct native-store or primary-owner claim. |\n3930|| Future plugin / any | ? / ? / ? | Disabled until a tuple-specific probe and acceptance record exist. |\n3931|\n3932|The release MUST NOT collapse WSL2 and native Windows into one row. An adapter\n3933|accepted in WSL2 does not establish native Windows support.\n3934|\n3935|## 9. Task-board integration\n3936|\n3937|### 9.1 Ownership boundary\n3938|\n3939|Task-board is both a provider-launch abstraction and a distinct persistence\n3940|boundary. <code>tb-sessiond</code> owns private Codex app-server/thread state,\n3941|Claude PTY state, reattach mechanics, provider resume, and goal bindings.\n3942|<code>ax</code> MUST NOT inspect manager databases, private session records,\n3943|provider process files, or authentication state.\n3944|\n3945|The only portable interface is the official\n3946|<code>urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>\n3947|contract. Its initial public creation surface is <code>launch</code>; its bundle\n3948|boundary uses <code>export</code>, <code>import</code>, <code>open</code>, and\n3949|<code>adopt</code>; its public lifecycle controls are <code>status</code>,\n3950|<code>stop</code>, and <code>resume</code>. Until\n3951|task-board advertises this exact bridge version and the required operations,\n3952|task-board takeover MUST report\n3953|<code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code>. Existing whole-board archive\n3954|commands are not a substitute.\n3955|\n3956|### 9.2 Official bridge command surface\n3957|\n3958|The required CLI facade is:\n3959|\n3960|~~~shell\n3961|task-board session launch --operation-id OPERATION_ID --request REQUEST_FILE --json\n3962|task-board session status --session SESSION_REF --json\n3963|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode snapshot --json\n3964|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode handoff --json\n3965|task-board session import --operation-id OPERATION_ID --bundle FILE --staging-root DIR --json\n3966|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode dormant-replica --json\n3967|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode fork --new-session SESSION_ID --json\n3968|task-board session adopt --operation-id OPERATION_ID --open-token TOKEN --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --json\n3969|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode graceful --control-token TOKEN --json\n3970|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode force --json\n3971|task-board session resume --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --profile standard|yolo --json\n3972|~~~\n3973|\n3974|Every command MUST print exactly one schema-versioned JSON result to stdout and\n3975|diagnostics to stderr. The bridge MAY use an internal local API, but the\n3976|semantics and bundle bytes MUST be identical.\n3977|\n3978|<code>REQUEST_FILE</code> is an owner-only, machine-local JSON file containing\n3979|exactly the logical <code>launch</code> request body below; the duplicated\n3980|<code>operation_id</code> MUST equal the flag. It contains no credential values\n3981|and MUST be removed after a terminal bridge result. Every mutating facade\n3982|requires the caller-supplied <code>--operation-id</code>; task-board MUST NOT\n3983|replace it with an internally generated value. This makes the exact invocation\n3984|repeatable after a lost response.\n3985|\n3986|The result envelope uses the bridge protocol version independently of the\n3987|bundle schema:\n3988|\n3989|~~~json\n3990|{\n3991|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge\",\n3992|  \"protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3993|  \"operation\": \"export\",\n3994|  \"ok\": true,\n3995|  \"body\": {\n3996|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-c180-72aa-8374-1234567890ab\",\n3997|    \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3998|    \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n3999|    \"bundle_path\": \"/var/folders/example/tb-session-bundle.tar\",\n4000|    \"size\": 4096,\n4001|    \"safe_boundary\": {\n4002|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n4003|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n4004|      \"boundary_ref\": \"tb-boundary-0198f4c8\",\n4005|      \"input_blocked\": true,\n4006|      \"foreground_idle\": true,\n4007|      \"background_idle\": true,\n4008|      \"open_processes\": 0,\n4009|      \"open_database_handles\": 0,\n4010|      \"store_generation\": \"tb-store:42\",\n4011|      \"safe\": true,\n4012|      \"blockers\": []\n4013|    },\n4014|    \"input_released\": true,\n4015|    \"source_control_token\": null,\n4016|    \"expires_at\": null\n4017|  }\n4018|}\n4019|~~~\n4020|\n4021|The success envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n4022|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>operation</code>, <code>ok = true</code>, and\n4023|<code>body</code>. On failure, it contains exactly the first four members with\n4024|<code>ok = false</code> plus <code>error</code> as a Structured Error and omits\n4025|<code>body</code>. Tokens returned by import, open, and handoff export MUST be unguessable,\n4026|machine-local, single-use base64url values of at least 256 bits and MUST expire\n4027|after 60 minutes. Tokens MUST NOT be replicated or written into immutable\n4028|bundles.\n4029|\n4030|Task-board bridge protocol <code>1.x</code> statically binds that failure object\n4031|to Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>; the facade has no separate error-schema\n4032|negotiation. A bridge executable that does not support protocol major 1 MUST\n4033|not emit a differently shaped failure as if it were a v1 result. Section 15.1\n4034|defines the caller's fail-closed mapping for incompatible or invalid output.\n4035|\n4036|The operations are:\n4037|\n4038|1. <strong>launch</strong>: create and launch the requested manager-owned\n4039|   provider through the public abstraction, bind it to the already-persisted\n4040|   epoch-1 ax lease, and return the public manager-session reference. It MUST\n4041|   record the caller operation before process creation, apply the persisted\n4042|   profile, and never return success for a blank substitute session.\n4043|2. <strong>status</strong>: return the public manager-session reference,\n4044|   provider ID, <code>running|idle|quiesced|stopped|failed</code> state, safe\n4045|   boundary evidence, and bridge capabilities without private state.\n4046|3. <strong>export</strong>: quiesce through manager-owned mechanics and produce\n4047|   an opaque, closed, integrity-checked bundle. It MUST NOT expose private\n4048|   records to <code>ax</code>. <code>snapshot</code> mode MUST release input\n4049|   before returning. <code>handoff</code> mode MUST leave input blocked and\n4050|   return a source-control token bound to the session and current fencing token.\n4051|4. <strong>import</strong>: validate and stage the bundle on the destination.\n4052|   It MUST NOT start a provider or claim ownership.\n4053|5. <strong>open</strong>: in <code>dormant-replica</code> mode, install the\n4054|   staged manager state without changing its provider identity; in\n4055|   <code>fork</code> mode, create a new manager/provider identity and\n4056|   independent goal-binding state for <code>--new-session</code>. Both modes\n4057|   return a single-use open token and MUST NOT accept agent input.\n4058|6. <strong>adopt</strong>: atomically bind that dormant state to the named\n4059|   <code>ax</code> session and current winning lease. Only the destination\n4060|   owner MAY adopt. A token MUST be consumed once.\n4061|7. <strong>stop</strong>: in graceful mode, consume the handoff source-control\n4062|   token, request the manager's normal stop path, and return process/store-\n4063|   closure evidence. If normal exit changed durable manager/provider state,\n4064|   the response MUST also produce a replacement closed bundle and its digest\n4065|   for the closure-only checkpoint. Force mode is tokenless, is permitted only\n4066|   through the separately confirmed <code>ax stop --force</code> path, and MUST\n4067|   mark the result unclean.\n4068|8. <strong>resume</strong>: validate the named winning <code>ax</code> lease and\n4069|   persisted profile, then either release a still-live quiesced manager or\n4070|   resume a stopped adopted/local manager session. It MUST return the public\n4071|   manager-session reference and resulting process/state evidence.\n4072|\n4073|For bridge protocol 1.0.0, each success <code>body</code> is closed and selected\n4074|by <code>operation</code>. CLI arguments shown above are the request contract;\n4075|every mutation command accepts the caller's required UUIDv7\n4076|<code>operation_id</code> and MUST reuse its durable result on an idempotent\n4077|retry.\n4078|The CLI spelling <code>dormant-replica</code> maps exactly to the logical JSON\n4079|enum <code>dormant_replica</code>; no other alias is accepted.\n4080|\n4081|| Operation | Exact logical request body | Exact success body |\n4082|| --- | --- | --- |\n4083|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4, provider_id:provider-id, launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt, task_element_id:string[1..128], board:Board Identity, board_goal:Board Goal&#124;null, native_goal_binding:bound&#124;prompt&#124;none, profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:BridgeLaunchPlan, workspace_paths:map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128], native_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null, launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt, state:running&#124;idle, input_enabled:boolean, ax_binding:BridgeBinding, capabilities:sorted unique launch&#124;status&#124;export&#124;import&#124;open&#124;adopt&#124;stop&#124;resume[8..8], native_goal_binding:bound&#124;prompt&#124;none}</code> |\n4084|| <code>status</code> | <code>{manager_session_ref:string[1..512]}</code> | <code>{manager_session_ref:string[1..512], provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128], state:running&#124;idle&#124;quiesced&#124;stopped&#124;failed&#124;dormant, safe_boundary:BridgeSafeBoundary, capabilities:sorted unique launch&#124;status&#124;export&#124;import&#124;open&#124;adopt&#124;stop&#124;resume[1..8], ax_binding:BridgeBinding&#124;null}</code> |\n4085|| <code>export</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],bundle_path:absolute-path,format:tb-session-bundle-v1,mode:snapshot&#124;handoff}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff, bundle_id:digest, bundle_path:absolute-path, size:uint53, safe_boundary:BridgeSafeBoundary, input_released:boolean, source_control_token:base64url-256+&#124;null, expires_at:timestamp&#124;null}</code> |\n4086|| <code>import</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,bundle_path:absolute-path,staging_root:absolute-path}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, bundle_id:digest, import_token:base64url-256+, staged_manager_ref:string[1..512], validated:boolean, expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n4087|| <code>open</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,import_token:base64url-256+,mode:dormant_replica&#124;fork,new_session_id:UUIDv7&#124;null}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, mode:dormant_replica&#124;fork, bundle_id:digest, dormant_manager_ref:string[1..512], open_token:base64url-256+, new_provider_identity:boolean, expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n4088|| <code>adopt</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,open_token:base64url-256+,ax_session_id:UUIDv7,lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0,lease_id:UUIDv4}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], ax_binding:BridgeBinding, adopted:boolean, state:quiesced&#124;stopped}</code> |\n4089|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],source_control_token:base64url-256+&#124;null,mode:graceful&#124;force}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], process_closed:boolean, store_closed:boolean, exit_code:int32&#124;null, safe_boundary:BridgeSafeBoundary, replacement_bundle_id:digest&#124;null, replacement_bundle_path:absolute-path&#124;null, state:stopped&#124;failed}</code> |\n4090|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],ax_session_id:UUIDv7,lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0,lease_id:UUIDv4,profile:standard&#124;yolo}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], ax_binding:BridgeBinding, native_session_ref:string[1..512], process_started:boolean, state:running&#124;idle}</code> |\n4091|\n4092|Normative tracked-prompt launch request body:\n4093|\n4094|~~~json\n4095|{\n4096|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0180-72aa-8374-2234567890ab\",\n4097|  \"ax_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n4098|  \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n4099|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n4100|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n4101|  \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n4102|  \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n4103|  \"board\": {\n4104|    \"kind\": \"local\",\n4105|    \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n4106|    \"remote_url\": null,\n4107|    \"extensions\": {}\n4108|  },\n4109|  \"board_goal\": null,\n4110|  \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\",\n4111|  \"profile\": \"standard\",\n4112|  \"launch_plan\": {\n4113|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n4114|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n4115|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n4116|    \"env_names\": [],\n4117|    \"env_literals\": {},\n4118|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n4119|    \"extensions\": {}\n4120|  },\n4121|  \"workspace_paths\": {\n4122|    \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/agent-session-manager-spec\"\n4123|  }\n4124|}\n4125|~~~\n4126|\n4127|Normative success body for that request:\n4128|\n4129|~~~json\n4130|{\n4131|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0180-72aa-8374-2234567890ab\",\n4132|  \"manager_session_ref\": \"tb-session-260819-example\",\n4133|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n4134|  \"provider_version\": \"task-board-qwen-prompt-v1\",\n4135|  \"native_session_ref\": null,\n4136|  \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n4137|  \"state\": \"running\",\n4138|  \"input_enabled\": true,\n4139|  \"ax_binding\": {\n4140|    \"ax_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n4141|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n4142|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n4143|  },\n4144|  \"capabilities\": [\n4145|    \"adopt\",\n4146|    \"export\",\n4147|    \"import\",\n4148|    \"launch\",\n4149|    \"open\",\n4150|    \"resume\",\n4151|    \"status\",\n4152|    \"stop\"\n4153|  ],\n4154|  \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\"\n4155|}\n4156|~~~\n4157|\n4158|<code>BridgeBinding</code> is exactly\n4159|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n4160|For <code>status</code>, the request member retains the historical name\n4161|<code>manager_session_ref</code> but accepts exactly one public reference\n4162|previously returned as <code>manager_session_ref</code> by launch/adopt or as\n4163|<code>dormant_manager_ref</code> by open. The success repeats that input\n4164|byte-for-byte. A staged reference is not status-addressable. Thus an adopt\n4165|response lost after token consumption is recoverable through the dormant\n4166|reference without inspecting manager-private state.\n4167|<code>BridgeLaunchPlan</code> is exactly the Section 5.1 Launch Plan shape,\n4168|including its closed <code>extensions</code> map and\n(more lines below)"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c649","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":383,"recorded_at":1780531400000761,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"709b66b4-5845-4833-bf83-46ebdc064c42"},"task_id":"709b66b4-5845-4833-bf83-46ebdc064c42","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"709b66b4-5845-4833-bf83-46ebdc064c42"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c64b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":384,"recorded_at":1780531400000763,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"call_id":"call_01a06f86f50b72a2abec2b4ad5ae4096","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(3868 line(s) above)\n3869|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n3870|| Pi | Session UUID/file; <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> or the configured <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR</code>/<code>--session-dir</code>. | <code>--session PATH_OR_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, <code>--resume</code>, <code>--fork</code>. | Adapter MUST snapshot a closed JSONL session and required non-secret companion data, map the destination cwd/session directory, validate the session ID, and resume explicitly. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until versioned cross-host fixtures pass. | <code>auth.json</code>, provider keys/tokens, extension secrets, live process state, locks, sockets, and caches. Pi 0.73.1 has no YOLO flag. |\n3871|| Qwen through task-board | The task-board bundle and manager-owned provider identity; there is no v0.2.1 direct claim and no v0.3.0 direct <code>ax-provider-qwen</code> claim. | Official task-board open/adopt only. | U for direct native materialization. A task-board prompt-mode bundle follows Section 9 and remains opaque. | All private manager/provider state except bytes included by the official bundle exporter. |\n3872|| Future plugin | Declared by plugin and exact probe. | Declared by plugin. | Every cell starts ?/disabled. Promotion requires Section 19 acceptance evidence. | Common exclusions plus plugin-specific exclusions. |\n3873|\n3874|Muse and Antigravity rows above are normative uses of the accepted\n3875|<code>TASK-260819-1ecd6x</code> evidence. The controlled Muse placement probe\n3876|does not create a supported import contract. Antigravity backend resolution is\n3877|native resume but not portable storage.\n3878|\n3879|### 8.3 Capability matrix\n3880|\n3881|| Provider | <code>native_resume</code> | <code>portable_store</code> | <code>managed_pty</code> | <code>appserver</code> | <code>task_board_primary</code> | <code>prompt_spawn</code> | <code>native_goal_binding</code> |\n3882|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3883|| Codex | A | C | C | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3884|| Claude | A | C | C | U for direct adapter | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3885|| Gemini CLI | A | C | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3886|| Muse | C by platform/version | U | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3887|| Antigravity CLI | C: backend realm required | U | C | ? | U | ? | U |\n3888|| Pi | A | C | C | U; Pi RPC is not claimed as this capability | ? | ? | U |\n3889|| Qwen through task-board | U direct | U direct | U direct | U direct | U | A through task-board | U |\n3890|| Future plugin | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? |\n3891|\n3892|For Codex and Claude, task-board owns app-server/thread or PTY mechanics,\n3893|reattach, resume, and goal binding. The direct Claude adapter therefore does\n3894|not advertise <code>appserver</code>. The task-board capability plane and\n3895|direct-provider capability plane MUST NOT be conflated.\n3896|\n3897|### 8.4 Provider/platform matrix\n3898|\n3899|Each cell is <code>native resume / cross-host materialization / managed\n3900|terminal</code>. Task-board-only behavior is stated separately.\n3901|\n3902|| Provider/platform | Status | Normative limit |\n3903|| --- | --- | --- |\n3904|| Codex / macOS | A / C / C | Resume and unrestricted flag are documented; portable store and PTY flush require adapter fixtures. |\n3905|| Codex / Linux | A / C / C | Same; exact distribution and filesystem fixture required. |\n3906|| Codex / WSL2 | A / C / C | Treat as Linux with a Linux store. Repositories SHOULD live below the WSL home, not a Windows-mounted path. |\n3907|| Codex / native Windows | A / C / C | Native CLI is documented. ConPTY, Windows store discovery, file locking, and sandbox mode MUST pass. Windows 11 is the release baseline; Windows 10 is best effort and requires ConPTY. |\n3908|| Claude / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 2.1.229 help confirms UUID resume and unrestricted flag; store transfer remains gated. |\n3909|| Claude / Linux | A / C / C | Provider family documented; distro/PTTY fixture required. |\n3910|| Claude / WSL2 | A / C / C | WSL is provider-documented; use Linux store and path rules. |\n3911|| Claude / native Windows | C / C / C | Windows 10+ with WSL or Git for Windows is documented, but native PowerShell/ConPTY and native store materialization require acceptance. |\n3912|| Gemini / macOS | A / C / C | Official session root, UUID resume, and session-file surface documented. |\n3913|| Gemini / Linux | A / C / C | Ubuntu 20.04+ documented; other distributions conditional. |\n3914|| Gemini / WSL2 | C / C / C | Linux inference; mounted-filesystem, auth, signal, and path-hash tests required. |\n3915|| Gemini / native Windows | A / C / C | Windows 11 24H2+ documented; PowerShell/ConPTY and path-hash tests required. |\n3916|| Muse / macOS arm64 | A for probed 0.1.0 / U / C | Narrow resume probe accepted; current 0.2.1 and full idle/cron fidelity remain unverified. |\n3917|| Muse / macOS amd64 | C / U / C | Artifact/contract exists; not executed. |\n3918|| Muse / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Official launcher artifacts; not executed. |\n3919|| Muse / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux-path inference only. |\n3920|| Muse / native Windows | ? / U / ? | 0.2.1 artifacts exist, but official launcher and persistence contract do not establish support. |\n3921|| Antigravity / macOS amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Resume works only when the authenticated backend realm resolves the UUID; <code>Stop.fullyIdle</code> is documented. |\n3922|| Antigravity / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; keyring/DBus and PTY tests required. |\n3923|| Antigravity / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux inference only; auth, path, signal, and locking tests required. |\n3924|| Antigravity / native Windows amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; ConPTY, data-root expansion, and file-lock tests required. |\n3925|| Pi / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 0.73.1 help verifies session surfaces and default full tool set. |\n3926|| Pi / Linux | C / C / C | Cross-platform Node/package behavior is plausible but exact 0.73.1 acceptance is required. |\n3927|| Pi / WSL2 | C / C / C | Treat as Linux only after path/signal/auth tests. |\n3928|| Pi / native Windows | C / C / C | Provider platform notes exist; exact 0.73.1 store, shell, and ConPTY behavior is unverified. |\n3929|| Qwen task-board prompt mode / any target platform | U direct; A only where task-board probe reports <code>prompt_spawn</code> | No direct native-store or primary-owner claim. |\n3930|| Future plugin / any | ? / ? / ? | Disabled until a tuple-specific probe and acceptance record exist. |\n3931|\n3932|The release MUST NOT collapse WSL2 and native Windows into one row. An adapter\n3933|accepted in WSL2 does not establish native Windows support.\n3934|\n3935|## 9. Task-board integration\n3936|\n3937|### 9.1 Ownership boundary\n3938|\n3939|Task-board is both a provider-launch abstraction and a distinct persistence\n3940|boundary. <code>tb-sessiond</code> owns private Codex app-server/thread state,\n3941|Claude PTY state, reattach mechanics, provider resume, and goal bindings.\n3942|<code>ax</code> MUST NOT inspect manager databases, private session records,\n3943|provider process files, or authentication state.\n3944|\n3945|The only portable interface is the official\n3946|<code>urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>\n3947|contract. Its initial public creation surface is <code>launch</code>; its bundle\n3948|boundary uses <code>export</code>, <code>import</code>, <code>open</code>, and\n3949|<code>adopt</code>; its public lifecycle controls are <code>status</code>,\n3950|<code>stop</code>, and <code>resume</code>. Until\n3951|task-board advertises this exact bridge version and the required operations,\n3952|task-board takeover MUST report\n3953|<code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code>. Existing whole-board archive\n3954|commands are not a substitute.\n3955|\n3956|### 9.2 Official bridge command surface\n3957|\n3958|The required CLI facade is:\n3959|\n3960|~~~shell\n3961|task-board session launch --operation-id OPERATION_ID --request REQUEST_FILE --json\n3962|task-board session status --session SESSION_REF --json\n3963|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode snapshot --json\n3964|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode handoff --json\n3965|task-board session import --operation-id OPERATION_ID --bundle FILE --staging-root DIR --json\n3966|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode dormant-replica --json\n3967|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode fork --new-session SESSION_ID --json\n3968|task-board session adopt --operation-id OPERATION_ID --open-token TOKEN --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --json\n3969|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode graceful --control-token TOKEN --json\n3970|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode force --json\n3971|task-board session resume --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --profile standard|yolo --json\n3972|~~~\n3973|\n3974|Every command MUST print exactly one schema-versioned JSON result to stdout and\n3975|diagnostics to stderr. The bridge MAY use an internal local API, but the\n3976|semantics and bundle bytes MUST be identical.\n3977|\n3978|<code>REQUEST_FILE</code> is an owner-only, machine-local JSON file containing\n3979|exactly the logical <code>launch</code> request body below; the duplicated\n3980|<code>operation_id</code> MUST equal the flag. It contains no credential values\n3981|and MUST be removed after a terminal bridge result. Every mutating facade\n3982|requires the caller-supplied <code>--operation-id</code>; task-board MUST NOT\n3983|replace it with an internally generated value. This makes the exact invocation\n3984|repeatable after a lost response.\n3985|\n3986|The result envelope uses the bridge protocol version independently of the\n3987|bundle schema:\n3988|\n3989|~~~json\n3990|{\n3991|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge\",\n3992|  \"protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3993|  \"operation\": \"export\",\n3994|  \"ok\": true,\n3995|  \"body\": {\n3996|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-c180-72aa-8374-1234567890ab\",\n3997|    \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3998|    \"bundle_id\": \"sha256:0af7b44e7063375a0f06e546fd820438c72607f191c14be78d35c8ffa109844f\",\n3999|    \"bundle_path\": \"/var/folders/example/tb-session-bundle.tar\",\n4000|    \"size\": 4096,\n4001|    \"safe_boundary\": {\n4002|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n4003|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n4004|      \"boundary_ref\": \"tb-boundary-0198f4c8\",\n4005|      \"input_blocked\": true,\n4006|      \"foreground_idle\": true,\n4007|      \"background_idle\": true,\n4008|      \"open_processes\": 0,\n4009|      \"open_database_handles\": 0,\n4010|      \"store_generation\": \"tb-store:42\",\n4011|      \"safe\": true,\n4012|      \"blockers\": []\n4013|    },\n4014|    \"input_released\": true,\n4015|    \"source_control_token\": null,\n4016|    \"expires_at\": null\n4017|  }\n4018|}\n4019|~~~\n4020|\n4021|The success envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n4022|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>operation</code>, <code>ok = true</code>, and\n4023|<code>body</code>. On failure, it contains exactly the first four members with\n4024|<code>ok = false</code> plus <code>error</code> as a Structured Error and omits\n4025|<code>body</code>. Tokens returned by import, open, and handoff export MUST be unguessable,\n4026|machine-local, single-use base64url values of at least 256 bits and MUST expire\n4027|after 60 minutes. Tokens MUST NOT be replicated or written into immutable\n4028|bundles.\n4029|\n4030|Task-board bridge protocol <code>1.x</code> statically binds that failure object\n4031|to Structured Error <code>1.0.0</code>; the facade has no separate error-schema\n4032|negotiation. A bridge executable that does not support protocol major 1 MUST\n4033|not emit a differently shaped failure as if it were a v1 result. Section 15.1\n4034|defines the caller's fail-closed mapping for incompatible or invalid output.\n4035|\n4036|The operations are:\n4037|\n4038|1. <strong>launch</strong>: create and launch the requested manager-owned\n4039|   provider through the public abstraction, bind it to the already-persisted\n4040|   epoch-1 ax lease, and return the public manager-session reference. It MUST\n4041|   record the caller operation before process creation, apply the persisted\n4042|   profile, and never return success for a blank substitute session.\n4043|2. <strong>status</strong>: return the public manager-session reference,\n4044|   provider ID, <code>running|idle|quiesced|stopped|failed</code> state, safe\n4045|   boundary evidence, and bridge capabilities without private state.\n4046|3. <strong>export</strong>: quiesce through manager-owned mechanics and produce\n4047|   an opaque, closed, integrity-checked bundle. It MUST NOT expose private\n4048|   records to <code>ax</code>. <code>snapshot</code> mode MUST release input\n4049|   before returning. <code>handoff</code> mode MUST leave input blocked and\n4050|   return a source-control token bound to the session and current fencing token.\n4051|4. <strong>import</strong>: validate and stage the bundle on the destination.\n4052|   It MUST NOT start a provider or claim ownership.\n4053|5. <strong>open</strong>: in <code>dormant-replica</code> mode, install the\n4054|   staged manager state without changing its provider identity; in\n4055|   <code>fork</code> mode, create a new manager/provider identity and\n4056|   independent goal-binding state for <code>--new-session</code>. Both modes\n4057|   return a single-use open token and MUST NOT accept agent input.\n4058|6. <strong>adopt</strong>: atomically bind that dormant state to the named\n4059|   <code>ax</code> session and current winning lease. Only the destination\n4060|   owner MAY adopt. A token MUST be consumed once.\n4061|7. <strong>stop</strong>: in graceful mode, consume the handoff source-control\n4062|   token, request the manager's normal stop path, and return process/store-\n4063|   closure evidence. If normal exit changed durable manager/provider state,\n4064|   the response MUST also produce a replacement closed bundle and its digest\n4065|   for the closure-only checkpoint. Force mode is tokenless, is permitted only\n4066|   through the separately confirmed <code>ax stop --force</code> path, and MUST\n4067|   mark the result unclean.\n4068|8. <strong>resume</strong>: validate the named winning <code>ax</code> lease and\n4069|   persisted profile, then either release a still-live quiesced manager or\n4070|   resume a stopped adopted/local manager session. It MUST return the public\n4071|   manager-session reference and resulting process/state evidence.\n4072|\n4073|For bridge protocol 1.0.0, each success <code>body</code> is closed and selected\n4074|by <code>operation</code>. CLI arguments shown above are the request contract;\n4075|every mutation command accepts the caller's required UUIDv7\n4076|<code>operation_id</code> and MUST reuse its durable result on an idempotent\n4077|retry.\n4078|The CLI spelling <code>dormant-replica</code> maps exactly to the logical JSON\n4079|enum <code>dormant_replica</code>; no other alias is accepted.\n4080|\n4081|| Operation | Exact logical request body | Exact success body |\n4082|| --- | --- | --- |\n4083|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4, provider_id:provider-id, launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt, task_element_id:string[1..128], board:Board Identity, board_goal:Board Goal&#124;null, native_goal_binding:bound&#124;prompt&#124;none, profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:BridgeLaunchPlan, workspace_paths:map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128], native_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null, launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt, state:running&#124;idle, input_enabled:boolean, ax_binding:BridgeBinding, capabilities:sorted unique launch&#124;status&#124;export&#124;import&#124;open&#124;adopt&#124;stop&#124;resume[8..8], native_goal_binding:bound&#124;prompt&#124;none}</code> |\n4084|| <code>status</code> | <code>{manager_session_ref:string[1..512]}</code> | <code>{manager_session_ref:string[1..512], provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128], state:running&#124;idle&#124;quiesced&#124;stopped&#124;failed&#124;dormant, safe_boundary:BridgeSafeBoundary, capabilities:sorted unique launch&#124;status&#124;export&#124;import&#124;open&#124;adopt&#124;stop&#124;resume[1..8], ax_binding:BridgeBinding&#124;null}</code> |\n4085|| <code>export</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],bundle_path:absolute-path,format:tb-session-bundle-v1,mode:snapshot&#124;handoff}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff, bundle_id:digest, bundle_path:absolute-path, size:uint53, safe_boundary:BridgeSafeBoundary, input_released:boolean, source_control_token:base64url-256+&#124;null, expires_at:timestamp&#124;null}</code> |\n4086|| <code>import</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,bundle_path:absolute-path,staging_root:absolute-path}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, bundle_id:digest, import_token:base64url-256+, staged_manager_ref:string[1..512], validated:boolean, expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n4087|| <code>open</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,import_token:base64url-256+,mode:dormant_replica&#124;fork,new_session_id:UUIDv7&#124;null}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, mode:dormant_replica&#124;fork, bundle_id:digest, dormant_manager_ref:string[1..512], open_token:base64url-256+, new_provider_identity:boolean, expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n4088|| <code>adopt</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,open_token:base64url-256+,ax_session_id:UUIDv7,lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0,lease_id:UUIDv4}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], ax_binding:BridgeBinding, adopted:boolean, state:quiesced&#124;stopped}</code> |\n4089|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],source_control_token:base64url-256+&#124;null,mode:graceful&#124;force}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], process_closed:boolean, store_closed:boolean, exit_code:int32&#124;null, safe_boundary:BridgeSafeBoundary, replacement_bundle_id:digest&#124;null, replacement_bundle_path:absolute-path&#124;null, state:stopped&#124;failed}</code> |\n4090|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,manager_session_ref:string[1..512],ax_session_id:UUIDv7,lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0,lease_id:UUIDv4,profile:standard&#124;yolo}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, manager_session_ref:string[1..512], ax_binding:BridgeBinding, native_session_ref:string[1..512], process_started:boolean, state:running&#124;idle}</code> |\n4091|\n4092|Normative tracked-prompt launch request body:\n4093|\n4094|~~~json\n4095|{\n4096|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0180-72aa-8374-2234567890ab\",\n4097|  \"ax_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n4098|  \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n4099|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n4100|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n4101|  \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n4102|  \"task_element_id\": \"TASK-260819-example\",\n4103|  \"board\": {\n4104|    \"kind\": \"local\",\n4105|    \"logical_id\": \"agent-session-manager-spec\",\n4106|    \"remote_url\": null,\n4107|    \"extensions\": {}\n4108|  },\n4109|  \"board_goal\": null,\n4110|  \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\",\n4111|  \"profile\": \"standard\",\n4112|  \"launch_plan\": {\n4113|    \"argv\": [\"task-board\", \"qwen\", \"TASK-260819-example\"],\n4114|    \"cwd_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\",\n4115|    \"cwd_relative\": \".\",\n4116|    \"env_names\": [],\n4117|    \"env_literals\": {},\n4118|    \"contains_secrets\": false,\n4119|    \"extensions\": {}\n4120|  },\n4121|  \"workspace_paths\": {\n4122|    \"0198f4c8-b080-7299-8273-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/agent-session-manager-spec\"\n4123|  }\n4124|}\n4125|~~~\n4126|\n4127|Normative success body for that request:\n4128|\n4129|~~~json\n4130|{\n4131|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-0180-72aa-8374-2234567890ab\",\n4132|  \"manager_session_ref\": \"tb-session-260819-example\",\n4133|  \"provider_id\": \"qwen\",\n4134|  \"provider_version\": \"task-board-qwen-prompt-v1\",\n4135|  \"native_session_ref\": null,\n4136|  \"launch_mode\": \"tracked_prompt\",\n4137|  \"state\": \"running\",\n4138|  \"input_enabled\": true,\n4139|  \"ax_binding\": {\n4140|    \"ax_session_id\": \"0198f4c8-9f60-7077-8071-1234567890ab\",\n4141|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n4142|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n4143|  },\n4144|  \"capabilities\": [\n4145|    \"adopt\",\n4146|    \"export\",\n4147|    \"import\",\n4148|    \"launch\",\n4149|    \"open\",\n4150|    \"resume\",\n4151|    \"status\",\n4152|    \"stop\"\n4153|  ],\n4154|  \"native_goal_binding\": \"prompt\"\n4155|}\n4156|~~~\n4157|\n4158|<code>BridgeBinding</code> is exactly\n4159|<code>{ax_session_id:UUIDv7, lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0, lease_id:UUIDv4}</code>.\n4160|For <code>status</code>, the request member retains the historical name\n4161|<code>manager_session_ref</code> but accepts exactly one public reference\n4162|previously returned as <code>manager_session_ref</code> by launch/adopt or as\n4163|<code>dormant_manager_ref</code> by open. The success repeats that input\n4164|byte-for-byte. A staged reference is not status-addressable. Thus an adopt\n4165|response lost after token consumption is recoverable through the dormant\n4166|reference without inspecting manager-private state.\n4167|<code>BridgeLaunchPlan</code> is exactly the Section 5.1 Launch Plan shape,\n4168|including its closed <code>extensions</code> map and\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
