{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c79f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":554,"recorded_at":1780531400001103,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"450e4f49-e168-482e-9026-26296e6d5b36"},"task_id":"450e4f49-e168-482e-9026-26296e6d5b36","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"450e4f49-e168-482e-9026-26296e6d5b36","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-20-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"PROVIDER-\\\\|PTX-\\\\|provider-manifest\\\\|provider-probe\\\\|provider-identity\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.md | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"Find normative fixtures in spec\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"124:| Provider manifest | <code>urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n125:| Provider probe | <code>urn:ax:schema:provider-probe</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n144:| Provider identity | <code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> | <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n2072:<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\\n2089:| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\\n2094:A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\\n2109:fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\\n2116:  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\\\",\\n2748:<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\\n2752:  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"urn:ax:schema:provider-manifest\\\",\\n2802:<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-probe</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>:\\n2806:  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"urn:ax:schema:provider-probe\\\",\\n3133:<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-POS</code> fixture. Their absence of every\\n3140:    \\\"schema\\\": \\\"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\\\",\\n3204:<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N1</code> adds\\n3206:<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\\n3208:is read. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N3</code> makes the source authority equal\\n3291:| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\\n3292:| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\\n3293:| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\\n3294:| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\\n3295:| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\\n3296:| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\\n3297:| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\\n3298:| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\\n3299:| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\\n3305:<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\\n3308:<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\\n3310:<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\\n3311:<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\\n3315:<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\\n3316:<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\\n3317:<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\\n3335:      \\\"schema\\\": \\\"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\\\",\\n4583:Session, event, lease, checkpoint, workspace-group, provider-identity, and\\n4953:Normative <code>PROVIDER-CAPTURE-POS</code> manifest returned by provider\\n4982:<code>PROVIDER-CAPTURE-N1</code> failure and MUST be rejected before object-store\\n5483:<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-MATERIALIZE-POS</code> cross-host fixture: the destination\\n5642:<code>PLAN-PROVIDER-ACTION-N1</code> (task-board action in a provider plan),\\n7416:| <code>MAT-PROVIDER-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=provider</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, provider source only, null workspace request | Null path/classification/replica/marker through every phase; provider transaction commits after owner resume |\\n8192:direct provider-identity or task-board manager-reference member becomes\\n11058:<code>ERR-PROVIDER-COMPAT</code>, <code>ERR-BRIDGE-COMPAT</code>, and\\n11060:v1 failure envelopes; <code>ERR-PROVIDER-MAJOR</code>,\\n11064:<code>ERR-PROVIDER-FIRST</code>, <code>ERR-BRIDGE-FIRST</code>, and\\n11931:| <code>AC-PTX-001</code> | Fresh provider processes prepare/status/commit/rollback through the same host-created object/transaction authorities; same-filesystem and path-disjointness checks pass or fail before mutation, and all five rollback reasons round-trip exactly. |\\n11932:| <code>AC-PTX-002</code> | <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> is the sole provider mutation idempotency key; a lost-response mutation retry that changes materialization ID, transaction ID, plan, authority, activation, or rollback reason returns <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and creates no second transaction root; <code>materialize-status</code> carries no operation ID and may evolve from prepared to committed or rolled back. |\\n12209:| Provider transactions could not survive fresh plugin processes safely | Sections 3.2 and 7.5 define host-created object-source/transaction authorities, exact durable layout, path disjointness, same-filesystem atomicity, restart lookup/retention, and all-operation authority passing; Section 10.6 journals the authority and Section 11.3 maps every rollback reason; <code>AC-PTX-001</code> covers cross-process recovery |\\n12219:| Provider idempotency had two keys | Section 7.5 makes <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> the sole mutation key and all IDs/authorities immutable mutation-retry input, while status is an evolving read without an operation ID; the <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-*</code> fixtures and <code>AC-PTX-002</code> reject a second root without freezing status |\\n12559:- <code>PROVIDER-CAPTURE-TRANSFER-1</code>: produce\\n12560:  <code>PROVIDER-CAPTURE-POS</code> in an isolated sink, independently verify\\n12563:- <code>PROVIDER-FIRST-CAPTURE-1</code> and\\n12564:  <code>PROVIDER-CROSS-HOST-1</code>: run capture with no destination members,\\n12565:  then execute <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-MATERIALIZE-POS</code> using disjoint\\n12568:- every <code>PTX-*</code> and <code>MJ-CRASH-*</code> provider/materialization\\n12577:- <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> and\\n12578:  <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code>: use a fresh plugin process for every\\n12581:- every <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-*</code> case after a lost response, proving a\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6825,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1707,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
