{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":574,"recorded_at":1780531400001143,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"call_id":"call_01a06f8794af77539c115ffa31cfe266","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(2059 line(s) above)\n2060|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2061|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2062|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2063|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2064|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2065|  \"extensions\": {}\n2066|}\n2067|~~~\n2068|\n2069|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2070|\n2071|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2072|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2073|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2074|\n2075|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2076|| --- | --- | --- |\n2077|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2078|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2079|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2080|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2081|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2082|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2083|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2084|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2085|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2086|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n2087|| <code>logical_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Member of the Session Record workspace group |\n2088|| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\n2089|| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\n2090|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Identifying owner host |\n2091|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2092|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2093|\n2094|A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\n2095|are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\n2096|is the sole provider-defined identity-data surface in version 1.0.0. It MUST\n2097|NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\n2098|terminal ID, or mutable cache selector. Structured or binary provider data\n2099|belongs in a content-addressed provider manifest, not this map.\n2100|\n2101|An absolute workspace path MAY appear only as source observation metadata. It\n2102|MUST NOT be part of the cross-host identity. The destination adapter MUST\n2103|derive native path keys from the destination workspace mapping.\n2104|\n2105|Normative negative fixtures are: unknown <code>identity_kind</code>; absent\n2106|<code>opaque_identity</code>; a map value that is an object instead of a\n2107|string; an absolute source path in that map; or an Antigravity\n2108|<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST\n2109|fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\n2110|for the other kinds unless that provider's Section 8 contract requires it.\n2111|\n2112|Normative example:\n2113|\n2114|~~~json\n2115|{\n2116|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n2117|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2118|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\n2119|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2120|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2121|  \"provider_id\": \"antigravity\",\n2122|  \"provider_version\": \"1.1.14\",\n2123|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=1.1.14 <1.2.0\",\n2124|  \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n2125|  \"identity_kind\": \"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n2126|  \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2127|  \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaad\",\n2128|  \"opaque_identity\": {},\n2129|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2130|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:45.000Z\",\n2131|  \"extensions\": {}\n2132|}\n2133|~~~\n2134|\n2135|### 5.6 Workspace Group Record\n2136|\n2137|The Workspace Group Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:workspace-group</code>\n2138|version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its closed top-level shape contains exactly\n2139|<code>schema</code>, <code>schema_version</code>,\n2140|<code>record_id:digest</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2141|<code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n2142|<code>display_name:string[1..128]</code>,\n2143|<code>members:WorkspaceMember[1..256]</code>,\n2144|<code>created_by_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, and\n2145|<code>extensions:object</code>. Subject and workspace-group IDs MUST be equal.\n2146|Members are sorted by <code>workspace_id</code>, and no two members may have an\n2147|equal or case-colliding <code>group_relative_path</code>.\n2148|\n2149|The record defines immutable workspace topology, not evolving session\n2150|membership. Exactly one schema-valid Workspace Group Record may exist for a\n2151|<code>workspace_group_id</code>. Two different record IDs with that same group\n2152|ID are <code>integrity_failure</code>; the group and every referring session\n2153|MUST park until the conflicting history is reconciled. Changing the workspace\n2154|member set or its logical identities requires a new workspace group and new or\n2155|forked Session Records; no group-update winner is inferred from timestamps.\n2156|\n2157|<code>WorkspaceMember</code> is a closed tagged union. No member-level\n2158|<code>extensions</code> map exists in 1.0.0; unknown members are rejected:\n2159|\n2160|| Tag | Exact members |\n2161|| --- | --- |\n2162|| <code>kind = git</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:git</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>repository_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>sanitized_remote_urls:sorted unique sanitized-git-URL[1..16]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_checkout&#124;separate_worktree</code> |\n2163|| <code>kind = managed_tree</code> | <code>workspace_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:managed_tree</code>, <code>group_relative_path:path</code>, <code>tree_identity:string[1..256]</code>, <code>repo_relative_cwd:.&#124;path</code>, <code>agent_project_config_paths:sorted unique path[0..256]</code>, <code>materialization_policy:shared_tree&#124;separate_copy</code> |\n2164|\n2165|A sanitized Git URL uses <code>https</code>, <code>ssh</code>, or provider-neutral\n2166|<code>git</code> syntax and MUST contain no password, token, query, fragment, or\n2167|machine-local file path. <code>repository_identity</code> and\n2168|<code>tree_identity</code> are logical labels, not absolute paths. Every cwd and\n2169|project-config path is relative to that member and MUST exist in the referenced\n2170|workspace snapshot when materialized.\n2171|\n2172|If multiple active sessions share a checkout or managed tree, takeover MUST migrate the whole\n2173|workspace group or materialize separate worktrees. It MUST NOT move one session\n2174|onto a concurrently mutated shared directory.\n2175|\n2176|Normative example:\n2177|\n2178|~~~json\n2179|{\n2180|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:workspace-group\",\n2181|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2182|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:3b366ca989681c63323c5de6db28198796aa913947ad3cd9456fc6dcee62b743\",\n2183|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n2184|  \"workspace_group_id\": \"0198f4c8-5b20-7c33-8c4d-1234567890ab\",\n2185|  \"display_name\": \"payments\",\n2186|  \"members\": [\n2187|    {\n2188|      \"workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2189|      \"kind\": \"git\",\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
