  \\\"recovery_evidence\\\": [\\\"recorded durable result\\\", \\\"session.status before retry\\\", \\\"canonical-identical request replay\\\", \\\"changed body refuses with idempotency_mismatch\\\"]\\ninternal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json:333:          {\\\"exit_code\\\": 3, \\\"codes\\\": [\\\"invalid_config\\\", \\\"idempotency_mismatch\\\", \\\"local_precondition_failed\\\"]},\\n===\\n66:- a general-purpose backup, secrets manager, or source-control system;\\n351:a core ownership, fencing, path-safety, secret-exclusion, or transaction fact.\\n374:| Provider identity | Provider ID, native durable handle, logical workspace mapping, and non-secret backend-realm fingerprint needed to resolve a native session. |\\n401:5. Provider credentials, environment secrets, authentication state, live PIDs,\\n492:    secrets are excluded.\\n1478:| <code>launch_plan</code> | Launch Plan | Closed shape below; sanitized and secret-free |\\n1490:| <code>env_names</code> | array&lt;string&gt;[0..64] | Sorted, unique names matching <code>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,127}</code>; values resolve only from destination-local state |\\n1491:| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\\n1492:| <code>contains_secrets</code> | boolean | MUST be false |\\n1496:values, inline credential-bearing URLs, response files containing secrets, and\\n1498:<code>env_names</code> is a destination-local lookup instruction, not a stored\\n1561:    \\\"env_names\\\": [\\\"OPENAI_API_KEY\\\"],\\n1562:    \\\"env_literals\\\": {},\\n1563:    \\\"contains_secrets\\\": false,\\n1593:    \\\"env_names\\\": [],\\n1594:    \\\"env_literals\\\": {},\\n1595:    \\\"contains_secrets\\\": false,\\n2088:| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\\n2095:are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\\n2562:No v2 table accepts a secret, endpoint credential, model token, auth root, or\\n2596:An arbitrary blob, raw command/argv, secret, token, endpoint credential,\\n2611:credentials, auth databases, raw evidence secrets, environment values, or live\\n2890:| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\\n3110:secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\\n3128:workspace ID and contains destination-derived non-secret cache-key data, never\\n3209:the credential root and MUST fail with <code>secret_policy_violation</code>.\\n3217:secret-policy violation and MUST discard the isolated sink without importing\\n3386:    \\\"env_names\\\": [\\\"OPENAI_API_KEY\\\"],\\n3387:    \\\"env_literals\\\": {},\\n3517:| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3875,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 969,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
