7-// internal/specdoc/SPEC.md at the lines named:\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-118-//\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-119-//\\tSPEC.md:218 \\\"map keys MUST be UTF-8 strings and MUST be unique\\\"\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-120-//\\tSPEC.md:221 \\\"floating-point numbers, NaN, Infinity, non-string map keys, and duplicate keys are forbidden\\\"\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-121-//\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-122-// encoding/json does not refuse such a document:\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-123-// it resolves repeats, and it resolves them differently depending on the decode\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-124-// target. A map decode keeps the last occurrence, a struct decode keeps the last\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-125-// occurrence, and a decode into a map-typed member such as details merges both\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-126-// occurrences into one map. So a Structured Error carrying \\\"retryable\\\": false\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-127-// followed by \\\"retryable\\\": true used to be read as retryable - a forged retry\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-128-// claim assembled out of two members neither of which a conforming writer could\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-129-// have emitted - and a repeated details resolved to the union of both\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-130-// occurrences, which is neither one. Two conforming readers of the same bytes\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-131-// disagreed, which is precisely the compatibility property this package exists\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-132-// to hold.\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-133-//\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-134-// The gate is the same one the CLI Result reader runs (cliresult.Decode), so\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-135-// both branches of a machine reading now enforce the same data model rather than\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-136-// one of them relying on the other to do it. It reaches every peer-supplied\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-137-// envelope through DecodeBound: provider, bridge, RPC, session-adapter and\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-138-// terminal-backend payloads are read here, so the duplicate-member shape is\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-139-// remotely reachable and is refused at the same place for all of them.\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-140-//\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-141-// Canonicalize's strict decoder settles more than duplicates - malformed UTF-8,\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-142-// lone or unpaired surrogate escapes, unescaped control characters in strings,\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-143-// trailing data after the top-level value, and more than 256 simultaneously open\\ninternal/axerror/decode.go-144-// containers. Measured against the mutant that deletes this call, it is the only\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8422,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2106,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
