{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000db1b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":3048,"recorded_at":1780531400006091,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"894170da-5fc9-4cc2-b53c-ad18d80ad557"},"task_id":"894170da-5fc9-4cc2-b53c-ad18d80ad557","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"894170da-5fc9-4cc2-b53c-ad18d80ad557","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(419 line(s) above)\n420|may be built outside the four constructors, and the observed code set must\n421|equal the closed three-code set. Section 7.1 citations in its tests resolve\n422|against the digest-pinned document in `internal/specdoc`, quoting the exact\n423|line each claim begins on.\n424|\n425|## Provider Plugin JSONL Protocol\n426|\n427|[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) implements the ax host side of\n428|the Section 7.2 provider plugin JSON-over-stdio protocol: one-frame JSONL\n429|transport, deadlines, size limits, stdout/stderr separation, operation\n430|dispatch, and status recovery. `Host.Call` is the production entry point.\n431|It frames one request envelope (`protocol`, `protocol_version`,\n432|`request_id`, `operation`, `deadline`, `body`), starts one plugin process\n433|per operation, enforces the request deadline, and interprets the single\n434|response frame. Unknown operations, stale deadlines, and unframeable\n435|bodies are refused with `invalid_config` before any process starts.\n436|\n437|Each stdout line must be one complete UTF-8 JSON object no larger than 8\n438|MiB; stdout carries the single response frame while diagnostics stay on\n439|stderr and never enter failure text. A recognizable foreign major yields\n440|`incompatible_protocol` without trusting the payload; every other\n441|unusable frame yields `provider_protocol_error`, both as local Structured\n442|Error 1.0.0 objects built without adopting any child-supplied code,\n443|retryable bit, details, or authority. A plugin that exceeds its deadline\n444|is terminated (as a process group on unix; direct-child kill on Windows)\n445|and reported as `provider_timeout`; a\n446|crash without a response is `provider_process_failed`. On success the raw\n447|body is returned for the operation layer; on failure the bound child\n448|error is returned itself. All six codes are pinned against the contract\n449|registry with their exact exits (3, 13, 6, 13, 13, 9).\n450|\n451|Dispatch covers exactly the 15 Section 7.5 operations in manifest order,\n452|derived from the pinned specification text, and refuses any other name\n453|without spawning. Status recovery interprets `materialize-status` bodies\n454|through the Section 7.5 state rules: unknown fails closed with\n455|`integrity_failure` for quarantine, prepared requires plan, token, and\n456|discovery, terminal states require plan and discovery with no token, and\n457|identity members must equal the requested transaction. Reads evolve —\n458|prepared under one envelope may be committed under the next — and each\n459|call starts a fresh process, so recovery observes durable state through\n460|the passed authority with no host-side mutation cache. Full request and\n461|success body vocabularies and mutation idempotency receipts belong to the\n462|conformance leaf of this story, not here; bodies cross this package\n463|opaquely except for the object-shape and status rules above.\n464|\n465|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n466|\n467|```bash\n468|go test ./internal/provhost -count=1\n469|go test ./internal/provhost -cover -count=1\n470|```\n471|\n472|The package derives its refusal inventory from its own source: every\n473|refusal constructor call site must have an exercised negative path, no\n474|Structured Error may be built outside the six constructors, no raw error\n475|may be minted, and the observed code set must equal the closed six-code\n476|set. Every refusal assertion names the arm it must reach (the refused\n477|member and the rule detail), so a gate deleted from a required-member list\n478|slides to a lower arm and reddens instead of passing silently. The\n479|rollback-token entropy floor is pinned at exactly 31 refused / 32 accepted\n480|decoded bytes, both frame-size bounds are pinned at exactly limit refused /\n481|limit accepted from both directions, and the operation registry is pinned\n482|against the Section 7.5 table in order. Refusal arms are derived from\n483|production source rather than listed: every frameFault literal,\n484|integrity detail, and parseMajor classification branch must carry a\n485|witness at the production entry, and every witness must name a derived\n486|arm, so a planted arm or a deleted branch reddens in either direction.\n487|stdoutCap is pinned at MaxFrameBytes+2 in both directions, with a\n488|maximal-frame-plus-junk probe through the production runner proving the\n489|probe byte is load-bearing.\n(more lines below)"}}}
