{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dbcd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06f86-1896-77b0-a64d-49a48c76fe78"},"sequence":3137,"recorded_at":1780531400006269,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3bc73467-9e0e-4b04-8606-b581be737d17"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a3e162ad-75c9-41f2-9abd-b9aeac3e098f"},"task_id":"a3e162ad-75c9-41f2-9abd-b9aeac3e098f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a3e162ad-75c9-41f2-9abd-b9aeac3e098f","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-05\n-\n-### 0435 — Provider JSONL host leaf round-2 rework: arm identity, exact bounds, production-site pins\n+## 2026-09-05\n+\n+### 0510 — Provider conformance-harness leaf: operation decoders, derived complements, inventory census 60 → 162\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-32jeti (final leaf of STORY-260830-3jqsx1). New `internal/provhost` operation layer: manifest (7.3), probe + capability gate (7.4/8.3), profile mapping (7.7), quiescence proof (7.6), SpawnPlan for launch/resume, Provider Identity Record + identify result (5.5), and the single `(operation, operation_id)` key (7.5), with Host.Call conformance sequences (manifest/probe/resume/identify/quiesce end to end, 21 fail-closed capability-by-status tuples with zero processes started, byte-identical lost-prepare retry, changed-body `idempotency_mismatch` passthrough, child-code passthrough table). Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- MECHANISM (leaf-2 item closed here): the derived refusal-arm inventory parses production AST — every `&frameFault` literal, every literal `integrity(...)` argument (with the `decodeStrictObject`-fault wrapper expanded over the derived frame detail set), every `parseMajor` rejection branch keyed by enclosing condition, and every literal first argument to the six refusal constructors — and checks both directions (every derived arm witnessed, every witness derived) plus a census floor. This leaf raised the floor 60 → 162 and added 102 witnesses, one per new arm.\n+- BLIND SHAPES (stated, not fixed): a one-line wrapper fronting a constructor and an aliased constructor at an unexercised site are both invisible to the arm walk and the site audit; both measured empty in this tree and neither shape was introduced. The file header's \"non-literal shapes never silent\" line was corrected: constructor non-literals are fault conduits by design, not obligations.\n+- CENSUS-FLOOR REASONING: the floor catches a silently truncated scan (empty, single-file, or short derivation fails even when every surviving arm is witnessed); the reverse witness check catches a deleted or narrowed production branch by orphaning its witness. Raising is routine with new refusals; lowering requires saying why.\n+- DEFECT (caught by the new tests, fixed before review): the first `DecodeQuiesceProof` draft omitted both open counts from the safe-rule disjunction — `safe:true` with `open_child_count:1` validated. The per-conjunct safe-lie fixtures (one violated fact each) caught it; counts now return through `checkQuiesceCounts` into the rule.\n+- COMPLEMENTS, NOT SAMPLES: 6 providers × 2 profiles swept; 4 statuses × 2 enabled swept for the probe rule, the pure gate, and one capability key, plus a per-key sweep over all 7 registry keys; keyed operations derived per-row from the Section 7.5 table (capture, materialize, commit, rollback, fork) with the 10 unkeyed operations refused in the same test; registries (operations, capabilities, platforms) re-derived from the Section 7.3 example.\n+- EVIDENCE: 26 narrowing mutants (order-skip-first, bound+1, grammar weakening, gate `&&`→`||`, disjunct drops, key widening, registry deletion), each presence-asserted, full-package run, cp-aside restore byte-verified, tree hash equal before/after: 24 killed on first run, 2 survived (order checks skipping index 0 — no fixture distinguished the first element), both killed after adding first-element-substitution fixtures. Final: 26/26, 0 survivors. `go test ./...` exit 0, `-race` on provhost exit 0, `go vet` and `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 unchanged (17/403, 74 cases — no ownership bindings added or claimed). provhost cover 86.4% (was 88.1%: new decoders add covered statements faster than the audit's constructor-error branches).\n+- BOUNDS (unchanged and restated): `provhost` still has no importers and imports no new package; no top-level `cmd/`; the ten leaf-2 survivors stay as stated (S11/S12/S13/U2 included — no test implies detached-descendant knowledge); S1's one-off ExecRunner fork/exec red stands recorded. New bounds: mutation receipts live in the transaction document/plugin (host holds no cache — cross-crash durability is the document's property); Section 8 cell values are evidence labels (host pins the fail-closed direction per tuple, not per cell); Section 8.2 store exclusions, commit/rollback result vocabularies, and remaining Section 7.5 request bodies are still opaque; literal secrecy and shell-string argv rules are structural, not content-admitted; record_id is shape-checked, not recomputed.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+### 0435 — Provider JSONL host leaf round-2 rework: arm identity, exact bounds, production-site pins\n"}}}
